s high in vitamin A were linked to a lower risk for squamous cell carcinoma.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/01/well/eat/foods-high-in-vitamin-a-may-help-ward-off-skin-cancer.html', 'snippet': 'Diets high in vitamin A were linked to a lower risk for squamous cell carcinoma.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Getting a lot of vitamin A in your diet is tied to a lower risk for squamous cell carcinoma, a common form of skin cancer, a review of studies has found.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/24/well/24well_pog_eat/well_pog_eat-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/12/24/well/24well_pog_eat/well_pog_eat-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/24/well/24well_pog_eat/well_pog_eat-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 512, 'width': 768, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/24/well/24well_pog_eat/well_pog_eat-superJumbo-v2.png', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/24/well/24well_pog_eat/well_pog_eat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/12/24/well/24well_pog_eat/well_pog_eat-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/12/24/well/24well_pog_eat/well_pog_eat-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Foods High in Vitamin A May Help Ward Off Skin Cancer', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vitamins', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin Cancer', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vitamin A', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Skin', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Diet and Nutrition', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fruit', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vegetables', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-01T09:00:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Eat', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Bakalar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bakalar', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/ffe554f6-0ee1-5901-9b57-d6e82c5909bb', 'word_count': 249, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ffe554f6-0ee1-5901-9b57-d6e82c5909bb'}, {'abstract': 'Don’t count individual leaves —look for breaks in the pattern of the plants. Search in shady spots.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/01/magazine/how-to-find-a-four-leaf-clover.html', 'snippet': 'Don’t count individual leaves —look for breaks in the pattern of the plants. Search in shady spots.', 'lead_paragraph': '“First, you have to believe that you’ll find one and trust that they’re there,” says Leslie Hirst, a visual artist and professor at Rhode Island School of Design who made a series of paintings that each include 1,024 four-leaf clovers she found. In Hirst’s experience, four-leaf clovers are more prevalent in the spring before the first mowing. Beginners should scan the edge of a patch, where the plants are less dense. Don’t get up close and start counting individual leaves. Instead, visually skim for what Hirst calls “ruptures in the pattern” — a four-leaf clover makes the shape of a square, while the typical three-leaf version appears as a triangle. Imprint the four-leaf image in your mind until you can see it even when you close your eyes.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '19', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06mag-tip-image1/06mag-tip-image1-articleLarge-v6.jpg', 'height': 585, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06mag-tip-image1/06mag-tip-image1-articleLarge-v6.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 585}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06mag-tip-image1/06mag-tip-image1-jumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 999, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06mag-tip-image1/06mag-tip-image1-superJumbo-v6.jpg', 'height': 1280, 'width': 1312, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06mag-tip-image1/06mag-tip-image1-thumbStandard-v6.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06mag-tip-image1/06mag-tip-image1-thumbStandard-v6.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06mag-tip-image1/06mag-tip-image1-thumbLarge-v6.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType':