[{'firstname': 'Leah', 'middlename': 'Hager', 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/7e070fa9-25a5-53bb-9fab-0ef631365911', 'word_count': 1231, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7e070fa9-25a5-53bb-9fab-0ef631365911'}, {'abstract': 'How the MSNBC host staked her show on Trump — and won the largest and most obsessive audience of her career.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/01/magazine/rachel-maddow-trump.html', 'snippet': 'How the MSNBC host staked her show on Trump — and won the largest and most obsessive audience of her career.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Rachel Maddow was trying to get to work. She only had to get from the glass door of her doctor’s office to the tinted-windowed S.U.V. that was idling at the curb, waiting to spirit her to 30 Rockefeller Plaza, but there was a hitch. Maddow had torn three ligaments in her left ankle — fishing accident — and one of those ligaments ripped off a piece of her bone, so now she was lumbering toward the sidewalk, her foot strapped into a boot, her lanky body bent over crutches that creaked and boomed with every hit to the sidewalk. In Manhattan, this had the effect of a kind of ritualistic drumbeat, alerting every liberal within earshot to her presence.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06-mag-maddow-cover/06-mag-maddow-cover-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 741, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06-mag-maddow-cover/06-mag-maddow-cover-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 741}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06-mag-maddow-cover/06-mag-maddow-cover-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 830, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06-mag-maddow-cover/06-mag-maddow-cover-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1659, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06-mag-maddow-cover/06-mag-maddow-cover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06-mag-maddow-cover/06-mag-maddow-cover-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06-mag-maddow-cover/06-mag-maddow-cover-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Is the Moment Rachel Maddow Has Been Waiting For', 'kicker': 'Feature', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘I’m Trying to Explain What’s Going On’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Maddow, Rachel', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MSNBC', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'News and News Media', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liberalism (US Politics)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Russian Interference in 2016 US Elections and Ties to Trump Associates', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trump-Ukraine Whistle-blower Complaint and Impeachment Inquiry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-01T09:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Amanda Hess', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Amanda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hess', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/98409742-7b8e-5406-bdef-333feaf75846', 'word_count': 6064, 'uri': 'nyt://article/98409742-7b8e-5406-bdef-333feaf75846'}, {'abstract': 'The E.P.A. recently said it would move away from requiring the testing of potentially harmful chemicals on animals. Do you support the decision?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/01/learning/is-animal-testing-ever-justified.html', 'snippet': 'The E.P.A. recently said it would move away from requiring the testing of potentially harmful chemicals on animals. Do you support the decision?', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Sept. 10, the Environmental Protection Agency said it would move away from requiring the testing of potentially harmful chemicals on animals, a decision that was hailed by animal rights groups but criticized by environmentalists and researchers who said the practice was necessary to rigorously safeguard human health.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/10/multimedia/10xp-animaltesting1/10xp-animaltesting1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/09/10/multimedia/10xp-animaltesting1/10xp-animaltesting1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/10/multimedia/10xp-animaltesting1/10xp-animal