rivacy Law. It Is Nowhere in Sight.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Vow to Pass Privacy Bill Goes Unmet', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Online Advertising', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Senate Committee on Commerce, Science, and Transportation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-01T23:26:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By David McCabe', 'person': [{'firstname': 'David', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McCabe', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91b1bbc0-142d-5ab5-bf2d-cd5ea20dddf0', 'word_count': 1200, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91b1bbc0-142d-5ab5-bf2d-cd5ea20dddf0'}, {'abstract': 'In the last three months, Bernie Sanders raised $25.3 million. Pete Buttigieg raised $19.1 million and Kamala Harris $11.6 million, at a time when donations signal viability.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/01/us/politics/democrats-q3-fundraising-numbers.html', 'snippet': 'In the last three months, Bernie Sanders raised $25.3 million. Pete Buttigieg raised $19.1 million and Kamala Harris $11.6 million, at a time when donations signal viability.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Senator Bernie Sanders has produced the biggest fund-raising quarter of the Democratic primary,