 friend Jamal Khashoggi was in September 2017, when he was settling into his self-imposed exile in the United States. We argued about politics over dinner at a steak house in Washington. We cracked jokes about my struggle with a small piece of steak and his ease at devouring a much larger choice cut.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/02/opinion/02Muslimi1/02Muslimi1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/02/opinion/02Muslimi1/02Muslimi1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/02/opinion/02Muslimi1/02Muslimi1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/02/opinion/02Muslimi1/02Muslimi1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/02/opinion/02Muslimi1/02Muslimi1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/02/opinion/02Muslimi1/02Muslimi1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/02/opinion/02Muslimi1/02Muslimi1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Jamal Khashoggi Was My Friend. His Murder Was a Warning.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Middle East and North Africa Unrest (2010- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Assassinations and Attempted Assassinations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Censorship', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Khashoggi, Jamal', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mohammed bin Salman (1985- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Middle East', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-02T05:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Farea al-Muslimi', 'person': [{'firstname': '', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/ff7fc65c-56e5-5ca0-b421-155a6a278697', 'word_count': 1241, 'uri': 'nyt://article/ff7fc65c-56e5-5ca0-b421-155a6a278697'}, {'abstract': 'A sci-fi serial killer movie is streaming on Netflix. And “Donnie Brasco” airs on Showtime.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/02/arts/whats-on-tv-wednesday-in-the-shadow-of-the-moon-and-donnie-brasco.html', 'snippet': 'A sci-fi serial killer movie is streaming on Netflix. And “Donnie Brasco” airs on Showtime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'IN THE SHADOW OF THE MOON (2019) Stream on Netflix. Mysterious, bloody, possibly paranormal murders come with an order of cheese steak in this hard-to-categorize movie. Set in Philadelphia, the film opens in 1988 with the grisly deaths of a steak-slinging diner cook, a concert pianist and a bus driver. Each person collapses on the job, blood streaming from their ears, eyes and mouths. Neck wounds point to a serial killer’s involvement. Seeing a chance to prove himself, a young police officer (played by Boyd Holbrook) throws himself into solving the bewildering case at the same time that his detective brother-in-law (Michael C. Hall, an expert in fictional serial killer stories onscreen) is doing the same thing. Where the story goes next, though, is more unusual than that premise might suggest — the relationship between investigators and killer (Cleopatra Coleman) becomes a decades-long affair that eventually involves time travel.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/02/arts/02tvcol-intheshadow/merlin_161475738_2d09c415-a80e-4d94-bc90-108ef558e65b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/02/arts/02tvcol-intheshadow/merlin_161475738_2d09c415-a80e-4d94-bc90-108ef558e65b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/02/arts/02tvcol-intheshadow/merlin_161475738_2d09c415-a80e-4d94-bc90-108ef558e65b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/02/arts/02tvcol-intheshadow/merlin_161475738_2d09c415-a80e-4d94-bc90-108ef558e65b-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/02/arts/02tvcol-intheshadow/02tvcol-intheshadow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/02/arts/02tvcol-intheshadow/02tvcol-intheshadow-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': 