ng-young-active-and-physically-fit-may-be-very-good-for-your-brain.html', 'snippet': 'Physically fit young adults have healthier white matter in their brains and better thinking skills than young people who are out of shape.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Physically fit young adults have healthier white matter in their brains and better thinking skills than young people who are out of shape, according to a large-scale new study of the links between aerobic fitness and brain health. The findings suggest that even when people are youthful and presumably at the peak of their mental prowess, fitness — or the lack of it — may influence how well their brains and minds work.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/05/world/physed-brain-image-promo/physed-brain-image-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/05/world/physed-brain-image-promo/physed-brain-image-promo-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/05/world/physed-brain-image-promo/physed-brain-image-promo-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 685, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/05/world/physed-brain-image-promo/physed-brain-image-promo-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1370, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/05/world/physed-brain-image-promo/physed-brain-image-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/05/world/physed-brain-image-promo/physed-brain-image-promo-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/05/world/physed-brain-image-promo/physed-brain-image-promo-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Being Young, Active and Physically Fit May Be Very Good for Your Brain', 'kicker': 'PHys Ed', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fitness Pays Off at Any Age', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Exercise', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Intelligence and Intelligence Tests (IQ)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Youth', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Brain', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Age, Chronological', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-02T09:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Well', 'section_name': 'Well', 'subsection_name': 'Move', 'byline': {'original': 'By Gretchen Reynolds', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Gretchen', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Reynolds', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3dd78774-27d0-5d79-89e2-a77f50b508d9', 'word_count': 832, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3dd78774-27d0-5d79-89e2-a77f50b508d9'}, {'abstract': 'The poet Reginald Dwayne Betts, whose new collection is “Felon,” on the writer who helped him come to terms with himself.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/02/books/lucille-clifton-reginald-dwayne-betts.html', 'snippet': 'The poet Reginald Dwayne Betts, whose new collection is “Felon,” on the writer who helped him come to terms with himself.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A decade after Lucille Clifton’s “Good Woman: Poems and a Memoir, 1969-1980” and “Next: New Poems” were both finalists for the 1988 Pulitzer Prize in poetry, I was a prisoner at Red Onion State Prison in Virginia, befriended by a brother with long locs, a knife stashed in the dirt on the rec yard and a copy of Michael Harper’s anthology “Every Shut Eye Ain’t Sleep.” The man’s name I’ve long forgotten, but Clifton’s poems in that book — all of them taken from her first four collections, also found in “Good Woman” — would follow me in a way rivaled only by those years in a cell.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '21', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/04/books/04Clifton/00Clifton-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 860, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/04/books/04Clifton/00Clifton-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 860}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/04/books/04Clifton/00Clifton-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 715, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/04/books/04Clifton/00Clifton-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1430, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/04/books/04Clifton/00Clifton-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/04/books/04Clifton/00Clifton-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/04/books/04Clifton/00Clifton-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Praise of Lucille Clifton', 'kicker': 'the enthusiast', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Her Heavy, Helpful Words', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Clifton, Lucille', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Race and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Writing and Writers', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-02T09:00:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Books', 'byline': {'original': 'By Reginald Dwayne Betts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Reginald', 'middlename': 'Dwayne', 'lastname': 'Betts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c6a02ffc-7ea1-53bb-82e1-5f1f003d0958', 'word_count': 1075, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c6a02ffc-7ea1-53bb-82e1-5f1f003d0958'}, {'abstract': 'Ombré manicures are everywhere. And you already have everything you need.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/02/style/nail-art-this-is-the-manicure-of-the-season.html', 'snippet': 'Ombré manicures are everywhere. And you already have everything you need.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This is important: The tonal manicure is everywhere. Unless your Instagram explore tab is stacked with nail art, you may have missed this fact. ', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/02/fashion/02SKIN-NAILS-1/merlin_161795664_c8f4c5fd-06c6-44f6-a2b6-dd582eca1365-articleLa