stract': 'A brief, incomplete, very quiet guide to the history of music’s negative spaces.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/02/arts/music/silence-classical-music.html', 'snippet': 'A brief, incomplete, very quiet guide to the history of music’s negative spaces.', 'lead_paragraph': 'One of the most arresting objects on display in the musical instruments galleries of the Metropolitan Museum of Art is a 2,000-year-old bell from Japan that was built to be mute. Dotaku bells such as this one still puzzle historians, but we know they were made without clappers and buried in earth, probably as part of a ritual designed to bless crops.', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/arts/06Silence-Music/06Silence-Music-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 599, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/06/arts/06Silence-Music/06Silence-Music-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 599}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/arts/06Silence-Music/06Silence-Music-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1022, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/arts/06Silence-Music/06Silence-Music-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2045, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/arts/06Silence-Music/06Silence-Music-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/06/arts/06Silence-Music/06Silence-Music-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth'