d', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Sifton', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sifton', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/527dfdae-4bae-5f66-b75b-60cd83037569', 'word_count': 778, 'uri': 'nyt://article/527dfdae-4bae-5f66-b75b-60cd83037569'}, {'abstract': 'The crash at the airport in Connecticut, outside Hartford, involved an antique military aircraft. The plane carried 13 people.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/02/nyregion/plane-crash.html', 'snippet': 'The crash at the airport in Connecticut, outside Hartford, involved an antique military aircraft. The plane carried 13 people.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Ever since they were used for bombing missions during World War II, B-17 aircraft have had legions of loyal fans. And as time passes, the chance to fly aboard one of these aircraft has become more rare.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'B-17 Plane From World War II Crashes at Bradley Airport, Killing at Least 7', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'World War II-Era B-17 Bomber Crashes Near Hartford, Killing Seven', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Hartford (Conn)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Aviation Accidents, Safety and Disasters', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Bradley International Airport', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-02T14:30:55+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Azi Paybarah and Christine Negroni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Azi', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Paybarah', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Christine', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Negroni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2b49de13-da44-5ac9-8441-a3417a954a81', 'word_count': 1179, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2b49de13-da44-5ac9-8441-a3417a954a81'}, {'abstract': 'The swift, negative response of Irish officials to the plan by the British prime minister suggested that it would not draw the two sides any closer to an amicable divorce.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/02/world/europe/boris-johnson-brexit-eu.html', 'snippet': 'The swift, negative response of Irish officials to the plan by the British prime minister suggested that it would not draw the two sides any closer to an amicable divorce.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MANCHESTER, England — Prime Minister Boris Johnson of Britain insisted on Wednesday that he loved Europe, even as he presented officials in Brussels with a new, detailed plan to pull his country out of the European Union by the end of this month.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/02/world/02brexit1/02brexit1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/02/world/02brexit1/02brexit1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/02/world/02brexit1/02brexit1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/02/wor