'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/a70ab710-c42f-5267-9cec-d164277f286f', 'word_count': 1263, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a70ab710-c42f-5267-9cec-d164277f286f'}, {'abstract': 'She has handed off her early works to an eager, energetic new generation.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/02/arts/dance/de-keersmaeker-fase-rosas-danst-rosas.html', 'snippet': 'She has handed off her early works to an eager, energetic new generation.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In her early 20s, the Belgian choreographer Anne Teresa De Keersmaeker created two dances that remain among her most distinguished: “Fase, Four Movements to the Music of Steve Reich” (1981), for two women; and “Rosas Danst Rosas” (1983), for four. The last time she brought these minimalist masterpieces to New York, as part of the Lincoln Center Festival in 2014, Ms. De Keersmaeker, then 54, was among the performers onstage, joining dancers in their 30s and 40s.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/03/arts/02rosas-notebook1/merlin_161919519_cf962ce3-50c2-40c6-b908-0aa00b41a055-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/03/arts/02rosas-notebook1/merlin_161919519_cf962ce3-50c2-40c6-b908-0aa00b41a055-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/03/arts/02rosas-notebook1/merlin_161919519_cf962ce3-50c2-40c6-b908-0aa00b41a055-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 680, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/03/arts/02rosas-notebook1/merlin_161919519_cf962ce3-50c2-40c6-b908-0aa00b41a055-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1359, '