d and Developing Countries', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Humane Society International', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'World Health Organization', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Instagram Inc', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Twitter', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Istanbul (Turkey)', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-02T19:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Didem Tali', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Didem', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Tali', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/5249ce77-c116-5fdb-a8c8-c577ac9f76ec', 'word_count': 1609, 'uri': 'nyt://article/5249ce77-c116-5fdb-a8c8-c577ac9f76ec'}, {'abstract': 'The teenage boy was sleeping nearly all day. And when he was awake, he felt like he was cut off from reality. What was going on?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/02/magazine/mysterious-sleeping-disorder-diagnosis.html', 'snippet': 'The teenage boy was sleeping nearly all day. And when he was awake, he felt like he was cut off from reality. What was going on?', 'lead_paragraph': '“I don’t know what’s going on,” the 19-year-old exclaimed in a panicked voice as his parents entered the nearly deserted emergency room of a hospital in Eau Claire, Wis. He was a freshman at the university there. A high school friend, now at the university with him, had called them with a strange story. She told them that their son had been uncharacteristically quiet for a couple of days — he had a terrible headache. But that morning, he felt well enough to go with her to pick apples. He had been a little out of it all morning, but suddenly he was totally gone — just standing in the orchard staring into space. He wouldn’t even respond to his name. That’s when she called his mother.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06mag-diagnosis-image1/06mag-diagnosis-image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 472, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06mag-diagnosis-image1/06mag-diagnosis-image1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 472}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06mag-diagnosis-image1/06mag-diagnosis-image1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 806, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06mag-diagnosis-image1/06mag-diagnosis-image1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1612, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06mag-diagnosis-image1/06mag-diagnosis-image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06mag-diagnosis-image1/06mag-diagnosis-image1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06mag-diagnosis-image1/06mag-diagnosis-image1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'le