mes.com/2019/10/03/nyregion/new-schools-nyc.html', 'snippet': 'The plan marks the first major expansion of schools since Mayor Bill de Blasio took office nearly six years ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mayor Bill de Blasio has decided to use about $16 million in private funding from an education organization backed by Laurene Powell Jobs, the widow of Steve Jobs, and from Robin Hood, a philanthropic powerhouse favored by Wall Street executives, to help open a host of new and restructured public schools in New York City. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '25', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/03/nyregion/03NEWSCHOOLS-print/merlin_142205010_6f681ad2-a07a-4f0d-b160-4ad132f52f5d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/03/nyregion/03NEWSCHOOLS-print/merlin_142205010_6f681ad2-a07a-4f0d-b160-4ad132f52f5d-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/03/nyregion/03NEWSCHOOLS-print/merlin_142205010_6f681ad2-a07a-4f0d-b160-4ad132f52f5d-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/03/nyregion/03NEWSCHOOLS-print/merlin_142205010_6f681ad2-a07a-4f0d-b160-4ad132f52f5d-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/03/nyregion/03NEWSCHOOLS-print/02NEWSCHOOLS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/03/nyregion/03NEWSCHO