], 'headline': {'main': 'Scouring Manhattan for the Right Rental. Which Did She Choose?', 'kicker': 'The Hunt', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Renting and Leasing (Real Estate)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Manhattan (NYC)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-03T09:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'multimedia', 'news_desk': 'Real Estate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joyce Cohen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joyce', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Cohen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Interactive Feature', '_id': 'nyt://interactive/c3cf74aa-ae65-551d-80e0-3d1bb290aee5', 'word_count': 0, 'uri': 'nyt://interactive/c3cf74aa-ae65-551d-80e0-3d1bb290aee5'}, {'abstract': 'Nostalgia for 70s era bohemia runs high.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/03/style/the-eve-babitz-revival.html', 'snippet': 'Nostalgia for 70s era bohemia runs high.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Eve Babitz doesn’t have a computer, and if you phone her, she is likely to hang up on you. Since the afternoon nearly two decades ago when she dropped a lighted match on her lap while driving home from lunch in her ’68 VW Bug, she has kept mostly to herself, holed up in her West Hollywood apartment with her cat and seeing select visitors. Now 76, Ms. Babitz is dimly aware of her surging popularity, particularly among young women, but aging hits burn victims even harder than it does the rest of us, and lately she has turned more inward. “All publicity is great,” she has told her sister, Mirandi Babitz, as Mirandi recalled recently, “but not really in your 70s.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{