, 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/03/climate/03CLI-BRITAIN6/merlin_159759612_384e5a02-fe49-4b4d-b85c-1e67538f942f-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Britain, Struggling With Brexit, Eyes Another Retreat. This One’s From Fossil Fuels.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'For Britain, the Clock Is Ticking on Carbon Emissions Deadline', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Environment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Great Britain Withdrawal from EU (Brexit)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Greenhouse Gas Emissions', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Great Britain', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Alternative and Renewable Energy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Electric and Hybrid Vehicles', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'London (England)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-03T09:00:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Climate', 'section_name': 'Climate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Somini Sengupta', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Somini', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Sengupta', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2da60358-c34b-5caf-9fbb-4d99556ed017', 'word_count': 1279, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2da60358-c34b-5caf-9fbb-4d99556ed017'}, {'abstract': 'The league thinks India could be its next billion-dollar market. But first it needs to convince young Indians to fall in love with the game.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/03/magazine/india-basketball-nba.html', 'snippet': 'The league thinks India could be its next billion-dollar market. But first it needs to convince young Indians to fall in love with the game.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The soupy morning air in one of the world’s most polluted cities had all but cleared by the time Saturday morning’s outdoor practice ended for the men’s basketball team at Ramjas College. If players had to wait out New Delhi’s smog, they would never practice, because there are few indoor courts in India. Ankit Hooda, a 20-year-old student who is one of the team’s best players, lingered on the court and laughed as his friend showed off a right ring finger that was dripping blood. Moments before, his teammate, Navdeep Grewal, had sliced the finger on the metal rim while dunking the ball. For Grewal, who is 19, playing this sport is a joy. Grewal is the son of a military man, firmly ensconced in India’s middle class. Hooda, however, is not from the same class. To him, basketball means much more.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06mag-indiannba/06mag-indiannba-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06mag-indiannba/06mag-indiannba-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06mag-indiannba/06mag-indiannba-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/magazine/06mag-indiannba/06mag-indiannba-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', '