GM was negligent in allowing the killer to stockpile weapons and ammunition at its Mandalay Bay hotel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The company that owns the Las Vegas hotel where a gunman opened fire from his room onto a country music festival two years ago, killing 58 and wounding hundreds of others, agreed on Thursday to pay up to $800 million to settle lawsuits filed by victims. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '12', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'MGM Agrees to Pay Las Vegas Shooting Victims Up to $800 Million', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Hotel Agrees to Settlement Over Massacre in Las Vegas', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Las Vegas, Nev, Shooting (October, 2017)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'MGM Resorts International', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Suits and Litigation (Civil)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mass Shootings', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Mandalay Bay Resort and Casino', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Paddock, Stephen C (1953-2017)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-03T15:18:13+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Richard A. Oppel Jr', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Richard', 'middlename': 'A.', 'lastname': 'Oppel', 'qualifier': 'Jr', 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/62c24fc2-cb7f-5671-9bc1-db8567e77900', 'word_count': 1070, 'uri': 'nyt://article/62c24fc2-cb7f-5671-9bc1-db8567e77900'}, {'abstract': 'Thanks to Brexit, for the first time in centuries Ireland has more power than its larger neighbor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/03/opinion/britain-ireland-brexit.html', 'snippet': 'Thanks to Brexit, for the first time in centuries Ireland has more power than its larger neighbor.', 'lead_paragraph': 'DUBLIN — When Boris Johnson visited Ireland’s prime minister, Leo Varadkar, in Dublin last month as part of a last-minute scramble to reach some sort of Brexit deal, the two leaders began their day with a media briefing on the steps of one of Dublin’s grandest buildings. In the Edwardian Baroque style, it was built by the British authorities while the Irish were intensifying their struggle for independence. “Fortuitously,” the Heritage Ireland website snarkily notes, “the complex was completed in 1922 and was available immediately to be occupied by the new Irish Free State government.” Rarely has the word “fortuitously” elided so much.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/03/opinion/03McKay1/03McKay1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/03/opinion/03McKay1/03McKay1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/03/opinion/03McKay1/03McKay1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/03/opinion/03McKay1/03McKay1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/03/opinion/03McKay1/03McKay1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/03/opinion/03McKay1/03McKay1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailw