zing control of the market, New Yorkers used tactics that helped leave the taxi industry in tatters and hundreds of immigrant drivers on the edge of ruin. ', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the fall of 2006, Chicago held an auction to sell taxi medallions, the permits that let people own and operate cabs. Hundreds of bids poured in, including some offering to pay much more than expected. The city raised millions of dollars. Officials declared the sale a success.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/20/nyregion/00nytaxi35/00nytaxi35-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/09/20/nyregion/00nytaxi35/00nytaxi35-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/20/nyregion/00nytaxi35/00nytaxi35-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/20/nyregion/00nytaxi35/00nytaxi35-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/20/nyregion/00nytaxi35/00nytaxi35-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/09/20/nyregion/00nytaxi35/00nytaxi35-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/20/nyregion/00nytaxi35/00nytaxi35-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘We Were Wiped Out’: New Yorkers Preyed on Chicago Cabbies', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'New Yorkers Preyed on Chicago Cabbies, Too', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Taxicabs and Taxicab Drivers', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Chicago (Ill)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Credit and Debt', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'LEVINE, MICHAEL J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garber, Symon', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Medallion Financial Corporation', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Capital One Financial Corporation', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Signature Bank', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Daley, Richard M', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Personal Bankruptcies', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-04T09:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metro', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brian M. Rosenthal and Alyssa Schukar', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brian', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/985db74d-203c-5b72-ae02-3e4c8c874a90', 'word_count': 4920, 'uri': 'nyt://article/985db74d-203c-5b72-ae02-3e4c8c874a90'}, {'abstract': 'Germany may be known for its beer, but it is also home to some 250 whiskey producers, almost twice as many as in Scotland.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/04/travel/germany-whiskey.html', 'snippet': 'Germany may be known for its beer, but it is also home to some 250 whiskey producers, almost twice as many as in Scotland.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Among drinks enthusiasts, Germany is famous for producing some of the world’s best beers. And a few of the country’s valleys have attained cult status among wine lovers — in particular, Mosel, Rheingau and the Ahr. German schnapps are pretty much a known quantity, while the country’s herbal bitters have an even broader recognition, or at least the standout brand Jägermeister does.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/04/travel/04Germany-Whiskey-Trail-slyrs2/merlin_160889073_c57aa854-37fa-4123-a97a-e882a18f4428-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/04/travel/04Germany-Whiskey-Trail-slyrs2/merlin_160889073_c57aa854-37fa-4123-a97a-e882a18f4428-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/04/travel/04Germany-Whiskey-Trail-slyrs2/merlin_160889073_c57aa854-37fa-4123-a97a-e882a18f4428-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/04/travel/04Germany-Whiskey-Trail-slyrs2/merlin_160889073_c57aa854-37fa-4123-a97a-e882a18f4428-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/04/travel/04Germany-Whiskey-Trail-slyrs2/merlin_160889073_c57aa854-37fa-4123-a97a-e882a18f4428-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {