 also scrawled “traitor” on his picture, placing suspicion on Hindu nationalists.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/04/world/asia/gandhi-memorial-ashes.html', 'snippet': 'Vandals attacked a Gandhi memorial and may have stolen some of his ashes. They also scrawled “traitor” on his picture, placing suspicion on Hindu nationalists.', 'lead_paragraph': 'MUMBAI — He is the revered father of Indian independence, and it was what would have been his 150th birthday. And yet, on Wednesday, vandals attacked a memorial to Mohandas K. Gandhi, painted “traitor” in lurid green across his picture, and may have stolen some of his ashes.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/04/world/04gandhi-ashes-1-promo/04gandhi-ashes-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/04/world/04gandhi-ashes-1-promo/04gandhi-ashes-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/04/world/04gandhi-ashes-1-promo/04gandhi-ashes-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/04/world/04gandhi-ashes-1-promo/04gandhi-ashes-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1364, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/04/world/04gandhi-ashes-1-promo/04gandhi-ashes-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/04/world/04gandhi-ashes-1-promo/04gandhi-ashes-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/04/world/04gandhi-ashes-1-promo/04gandhi-ashes-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Did Vandals Steal Gandhi’s Ashes From an Indian Memorial?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Gandhi at 150: Site Attacked, and Ashes Gone', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Hinduism', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Vandalism', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gandhi, Mohandas K', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Modi, Narendra', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-04T09:40:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'World', 'subsection_name': 'Asia Pacific', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeffrey Gettleman and Sameer Yasir', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeffrey', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Gettleman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Sameer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Yasir', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/24b09178-4d0f-51e2-afa0-203053fd7f32', 'word_count': 726, 'uri': 'nyt://article/24b09178-4d0f-51e2-afa0-203053fd7f32'}, {'abstract': 'He set out to show that regardless of the barriers, he could fulfill his God-given potential. Struggle by struggle, he did.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/04/opinion/sunday/susan-rice-tough-love.html', 'snippet': 'He set out to show that regardless of the barriers, he could fulfill his God-given potential. Struggle by struggle, he did.', 'lead_paragraph': 'My father, Emmett Rice, was drafted into military service at the height of World War II and spent four and a half years in uniform, first as an enlisted man and ultimately as an officer with the rank of captain. Called up by the Army Air Force, he was sent to a two-part officer training program, which began in Miami and was completed at Harvard Business School — where he learned “statistical control” and “quantitative management,” a specialized form of accounting in an unusual program designed to build on his business background.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/opinion/06Rice1/06Rice1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 433, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/06/opinion/06Rice1/06Rice1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 433}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/opinion/06Rice1/06Rice1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 739, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/opinion/06Rice1/06Rice1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1478, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/opinion/06Rice1/06Rice1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/06/opinion/06Rice1/06Rice1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/opinion/06Rice1/06Rice1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'wi