'kicker': 'In her words', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Women and Girls', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Banking and Financial Institutions', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wages and Salaries', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-04T16:36:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Gender', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Kristin Wong', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Kristin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wong', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/48a15847-541b-5816-98c2-f821c2b148d9', 'word_count': 857, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48a15847-541b-5816-98c2-f821c2b148d9'}, {'abstract': 'At least 401 pro-government forces and 161 civilians have been killed in Afghanistan so far this month.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/04/magazine/afghan-war-casualty-report-october-2019.html', 'snippet': 'At least 401 pro-government forces and 161 civilians have been killed in Afghanistan so far this month.', 'lead_paragraph': 'At least 76 pro-government forces and 18 civilians were killed in Afghanistan during the past week. The deadliest attack took place Jowzjan Province, where a Taliban Red Unit attacked the Bala Hisar military base in Aqcha District, killing 20 soldiers, three pro-government militia members and one police officer. An additional five soldiers were taken prisoner, and 10 security forces were wounded in the course of the three-hour battle. The Taliban also seized four Humvees and 29 weapons from the base, which was recaptured after reinforcements arrived. In Takhar Province, insurgents attacked two security outposts in the villages of Qorogh and Khwaja Bandkasha, killing five police special forces and five pro-government militia members. Local authorities claimed that 12 Taliban members were also killed in the clash.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/magazine/10atwar-casualtyreport/merlin_162314832_f20e0deb-6588-4007-95f1-2d51ad464d9a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/10/magazine/10atwar-casualtyreport/merlin_162314832_f20e0deb-6588-4007-95f1-2d51ad464d9a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/magazine/10atwar-casualtyreport/merlin_162314832_f20e0deb-6588-4007-95f1-2d51ad464d9a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/magazine/10atwar-casualtyreport/merlin_162314832_f20e0deb-6588-4007-95f1-2d51ad464d9a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/magazine/10atwar-casualtyreport/10atwar-casualtyreport-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/10/magazine/10atwar-casualtyreport/10atwar-casualtyreport-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/magazine/10atwar-casualtyreport/10atwar-casualtyreport-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Afghan War Casualty Report: October 2019', 'kicker': 'at w