agraph': 'WASHINGTON — President Trump’s public call for the Chinese government to investigate a political rival could complicate next week’s trade talks, which are set to resume Thursday when American and Chinese negotiators meet in Washington to see if they can find a path to a trade deal.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/04/business/00CHINATRADE-02/merlin_162115044_3899a2a2-32cb-4aaa-94b5-16f27536cda4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/04/business/00CHINATRADE-02/merlin_162115044_3899a2a2-32cb-4aaa-94b5-16f27536cda4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/04/business/00CHINATRADE-02/merlin_162115044_3899a2a2-32cb-4aaa-94b5-16f27536cda4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/04/business/00CHINATRADE-02/merlin_162115044_3899a2a2-32cb-4aaa-94b5-16f27536cda4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/04/business/00CHINATRADE-02/merlin_162115044_3899a2a2-32cb-4aaa-94b5-16f27536cda4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/04/business/00CHINATRADE-02/merlin_162115044_3899a2a2-32cb-4aaa-94b5-16f27536cda4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'