46-5c9f-b04f-d80e7c562f7c'}, {'abstract': 'The Nationals treated Game 2 of their National League division series as a must-win, calling on their 35-year-old starter to pitch out of the bullpen and help tie the series.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/05/sports/baseball/max-scherzer-nationals-dodgers.html', 'snippet': 'The Nationals treated Game 2 of their National League division series as a must-win, calling on their 35-year-old starter to pitch out of the bullpen and help tie the series.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LOS ANGELES — Max Scherzer said he had not even worked up a sweat when he trotted out of the Washington Nationals’ bullpen late Friday night. He’s used to warming up when the sun is still out, after all.', 'print_section': 'SP', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/sports/06dodgers-folo/merlin_162152721_d6b5decc-8474-4e86-a699-ebe0e220c5bc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 817, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/06/sports/06dodgers-folo/merlin_162152721_d6b5decc-8474-4e86-a699-ebe0e220c5bc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 817}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/sports/06dodgers-folo/merlin_162152721_d6b5decc-8474-4e86-a699-ebe0e220c5bc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 753, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/sports/06dodgers-folo/merlin_162152721_d6b5decc-8474-4e86-a699-ebe0e220c5bc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1505, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/sports/06dodgers-folo/merlin_162152721_d6b5decc-8474-4e86-a699-ebe0e220c5bc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/06/sports/06dodgers-folo/merlin_162152721_d6b5decc-8474-4e86-a699-ebe0e220c5bc-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/06/sports/06dodgers-folo/merlin_162152721_d6b5decc-8474-4e86-a699-ebe0e220c5bc-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Max Scherzer Stifles the Dodgers in a Rare Relief Outing', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Appearance As Setup Man, Nationals’ Ace Mows Down 3', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Playoff Games', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Los Angeles Dodgers', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Nationals', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scherzer, Max', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Martinez, Dave', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Strasburg, Stephen', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-05T15:00:05+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jill Painter Lopez', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jill', 'middlename': 'Painter', 'lastname': 'Lopez', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f598d9e1-c652-538a-b95c-cb5f5087fe97', 'word_count': 849, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f598d9e1-c652-538a-b95c-cb5f5087fe97'}, {'abstract': 'They signed open letters, dedicated a special magazine issue to criticism of him and swore he would tear at the fabric of this nation. Now they have become the president’s strongest defenders.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/05/us/politics/never-trumper-republicans.html', 'snippet': 'They signed open letters, dedicated a special magazine issue to criticism of him and swore he would tear at the fabric of this nation. Now they have become the president’s strongest defenders.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — In 2016, Erick Erickson could not have been clearer. Donald Trump was “a racist” and “a fascist.” It was no wonder, Mr. Erickson wrote, that “so many people with swastikas in their Twitter profile pics” supported him. “I will not vote for Donald Trump. Ever,” he insisted, adding his voice to the chorus of Never Trump Republicans.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '15', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/05/us/politics/05nevermindtrumpers1/merlin_162143790_b57753d7-747a-49ef-b5d7-5f447ea56c77-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/05/us/politics/05nevermindtrumpers1/merlin_162143790_b57753d7-747a-49ef-b5d7-5f447ea56c77-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/05/us/politics/05nevermindtrumpers1/merlin_162143790_b57753d7-747a-49ef-b5d7-5f447ea56c77-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/05/us/politics/05nevermindtrumpers1/merlin_162143790_b57753d7-747a-49ef-b5d7-5f447ea56c77-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/05/us/politics/05nevermindtrumpers1/05nevermindtrumpers1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/05/us/politics/05nevermindtrumpers1/05nevermindtrumpers1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/05/us/politics/05nevermindtrumpers1/05nevermindtrumpers1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The ‘Never Trump’ Coalition That Decided Eh, Never Mind, He’s Fine', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A ‘Never Trump’ Coalition’s New Point of View: Never Mind, He’s Fine', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2016', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Beck, Glenn', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bozell, L Brent', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Erickson, Erick', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Graham, Lindsey', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-05T15:01:41+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/450b967a-f7ad-5893-9c2e-5b9cf4db89ec', 'word_count': 1324, 'uri': 'nyt://article/450b967a-f7ad-5893-9c2e-5b9cf4db89ec'}, {'abstract': 'Adam Grant on why we need to rethink “The Giving Tree,” and more from NYT Parenting this week.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/05/parenting/adam-grant-giving-tree.html', 'snippet': 'Adam Grant on why we need to rethink “The Giving Tree,” and more from NYT Parenting this week.', 'lead_paragraph': 'This week, Adam Grant and Allison Sweet Grant told us we need to talk about “The Giving Tree.” Why? Because “if you assume the story is about generosity, it’s easy to learn the wrong lessons: that it’s O.K. for a child to take selfishly, and that adults should give until it hurts — and keep giving until they literally have nothing left to offer.” Welp. Speaking of giving all of yourself to all of the things, we published our guide to time management for new parents who go back to work. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/30/multimedia/parenting-generosity/parenting-generosity-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 750, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/09/30/multimedia/parenting-generosity/parenting-generosity-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 750}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/30/multimedia/parenting-generosity/parenting-generosity-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 820, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, '