he name of progress.', 'lead_paragraph': 'NOVO PROGRESSO, BRAZIL — In early August, Adecio Piran wrote an article for this Amazon town’s news website announcing a “Day of Fire,” to be started on August 10. The post suggested a coordinated criminal effort among local landowners and cattle ranchers to burn newly cleared rainforest — much of it on public land. The unnamed organizers of the collective action, Mr. Piran wrote, wanted to draw the attention of President Jair Bolsonaro.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Threats and Promises in Brazil’s Lawless Amazon', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Land Use Policies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brazil', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Novo Progresso (Brazil)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bolsonaro, Jair (1955- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-06T09:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Foreign', 'section_name': 'Video', 'byline': {'original': 'By Brent McDonald', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Brent', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'McDonald', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/de03b250-840f-5834-9828-a75b4b737de9', 'word_count': 710, 'uri': 'nyt://article/de03b250-840f-5834-9828-a75b4b737de9'}, {'abstract': 'Instagram! iHeartRadio! Email! The veteran television personality is back with a desire for your little screens.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/06/style/what-is-katie-couric-doing-now.html', 'snippet': 'Instagram! iHeartRadio! Email! The veteran televisi