_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/07/t-magazine/supper-clubs.html', 'snippet': 'Once a mainstay of midcentury dining, the convivial establishments have reappeared, even as the meaning of “all-American” has become more complicated.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE LIGHTS ARE dim, set to eternal dusk. You enter and blink. If there are booths, they should be plush: Naugahyde or brocade limned in gold. Napkins are linen, tables likely cloaked. Maybe a Persian rug lies underfoot. Taxidermied animal heads peer from the walls. From your seat, you might see a living white-tailed deer out the window; like you, it is ready to feed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/07/t-magazine/07tmag-supperclubs-slide-IHO3/07tmag-supperclubs-slide-IHO3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 498, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/07/t-magazine/07tmag-supperclubs-slide-IHO3/07tmag-supperclubs-slide-IHO3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 498}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/07/t-magazine/07tmag-supperclubs-slide-IHO3/07tmag-supperclubs-slide-IHO3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 850, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/07/t-magazine/07tmag-supperclubs-slide-IHO3/07tmag-supperclubs-slide-IHO3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1645, 'width': 1982, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/07/t-magazine/07tmag-supperclubs-slide-IHO3/07tmag-supperclubs-slide-IHO3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {