 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Restaurants', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Beatrice Inn (Manhattan, NY, Restaurant)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Feldmar, Jamie', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-08T00:33:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2fcc5cce-54de-5de6-82c1-9fb205b58104', 'word_count': 197, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2fcc5cce-54de-5de6-82c1-9fb205b58104'}, {'abstract': 'The spice shop La Boîte adds a food-friendly amaro to the spirits it makes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/07/dining/la-boite-amaro.html', 'snippet': 'The spice shop La Boîte adds a food-friendly amaro to the spirits it makes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Those who have yet to embrace amari — the hyper-trendy bitter aperitifs originally from Italy but now concocted far and wide — might consider starting with the new one from La Boîte, the New York spice specialists, made by Cardinal Spirits of Bloomington, Ind. Lior Lev Sercarz, the owner of La Boîte, developed this amaro to be food-friendly, using culinary spices (his métier) in a base of distilled red wine. The result is mellower than most and can be sipped on its own, though a fortifying splash of gin or vodka would not be a mistake. The reddish-amber spirit, 40 proof, is slightly smoky and tinged with orange zest and anise.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/09/dining/07burner5/07burner5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 880, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/09/dining/07burner5/07burner5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 880}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/09/dining/07burner5/07burner5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 699, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/09/dining/07burner5/07burner5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1397, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/09/dining/07burner5/07burner5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/09/dining/07burner5/07burner5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/09/dining/07burner5/07burner5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'An Amaro From a Spice Master', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Sip: A Food-Friendly Amaro  From a Spice Master', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Spices', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liquor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sercarz, Lior Lev', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'La Boite (Manhattan, NY)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-08T00:34:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/04b7ca56-8ca9-50a4-aa86-c18a4ac89a19', 'word_count': 155, 'uri': 'nyt://article/04b7ca56-8ca9-50a4-aa86-c18a4ac89a19'}, {'abstract': 'For the pastrami superfan, a carving board made from the famed deli’s wooden countertop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/07/dining/cutting-board-katzs-deli.html', 'snippet': 'For the pastrami superfan, a carving board made from the famed deli’s wooden countertop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From time to time, the wooden countertops at Katz’s Delicatessen on the Lower East Side require replacing. The owners have now hit upon a way to recycle the used ones. They’re chopping them up and selling them, stamped with the Katz’s logo, as carving and serving boards for the home. Each one is 14 inches by 10 inches, one and a half inches thick and heavy.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/09/dining/07burner6/07burner6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/09/dining/07burner6/07burner6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/09/dining/07burner6/07burner6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/09/dining/07burner6/07burner6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/09/dining/07burner6/07burner6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/09/dining/07burner6/07burner6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/09/dining/07burner6/07burner6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Own a Piece of Katz’s Deli', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Cherish: Own a Piece Of Katz’s Deli', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Tableware', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cookware', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Delicatessens', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Katz's Delicatessen (Manhattan, NY)", 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-08T00:39:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/256fe971-43d6-55eb-897b-859eb54c779d', 'word_count': 97, 'uri': 'nyt://article/256fe971-43d6-55eb-897b-859eb54c779d'}, {'abstract': 'These new frozen breaded pork cutlets are made from heritage pork and prepared by a local butcher.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/07/dining/heritage-foods-breaded-pork-cutlet.html', 'snippet': 'These new frozen breaded pork cutlets are made from heritage pork and prepared by a local butcher.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Heritage Foods has come up with an easy, high-quality item for dinner: breaded pork cutlets (scaloppine), ready to sizzle in a pan and serve. (They come frozen but defrost in no time.) The results are tasty, quite tender and could be finished with a tangle of arugula salad, used Parm-style or topped with sautéed peppers and onions. The meat is cut from heritage pork porterhouse steaks, something you’re not likely to find in your neighborhood supermarket or even most butchers, and prepared by Pepe Giocoli, who owns Parma Sausage in Paterson, N.J.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/09/dining/07burner3/07burner3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 401, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/09/dining/07burner3/07burner3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 401}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/09/dining/07burner3/07burner3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 684, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/09/dining/07burner3/07burner3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1367, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/09/dining/07burner3/07burner3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/09/dining/07burner3/07burner3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image'