times.com/2019/10/08/world/americas/ecuador-protests-president.html', 'snippet': 'The move came after six days of protests against austerity measures, including the end of a fuel subsidy. Demonstrators clashed with the police and looted businesses.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GUAYAQUIL, Ecuador — President Lenín Moreno of Ecuador moved the seat of his government from Quito, the capital, to a coastal city more than 150 miles away late Monday in an attempt to protect his government from the large protests against austerity that have racked the country over the past week.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/08/world/08Ecuador1/merlin_162361044_5e151d29-b4f5-454a-b391-d0f3794ad5ee-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 388, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/08/world/08Ecuador1/merlin_162361044_5e151d29-b4f5-454a-b391-d0f3794ad5ee-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 388}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/08/world/08Ecuador1/merlin_162361044_5e151d29-b4f5-454a-b391-d0f3794ad5ee-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 662, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/08/world/08Ecuador1/merlin_162361044_5e151d29-b4f5-454a-b391-d0f3794ad5ee-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1325, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/08/world/08Ecuador1/merlin_162361044_5e151d29-b4f5-454a-b391-d0f3794ad5ee-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'imag