 Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Younger (TV Program)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Money Heist (TV Program)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Prime Suspect (TV Program)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Jack Irish (TV Program)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Missing (TV Program)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-09T14:35:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Margaret Lyons', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Margaret', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Lyons', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fc926315-63e7-55d7-9c43-7ff243a266af', 'word_count': 962, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fc926315-63e7-55d7-9c43-7ff243a266af'}, {'abstract': 'A teenage chambermaid living under the rule of Francisco Franco fights for justice, and finds love, in “The Fountains of Silence.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/09/books/review/ruta-sepetys-fountains-of-silence.html', 'snippet': 'A teenage chambermaid living under the rule of Francisco Franco fights for justice, and finds love, in “The Fountains of Silence.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'Spain under Francisco Franco is as dystopian a setting as Margaret Atwood’s Gilead in Ruta Sepetys’s suspenseful, romantic and timely new work of historical fiction, THE FOUNTAINS OF SILENCE (Philomel, 512 pp., $18.99; ages 12 and up). It’s 1957, but Franco’s isolationist policies and a powerful Catholic Church ensure that Spanish women are treated like chattel, Spanish babies lack basic medical care and Republican sympathizers end their days laboring like slaves. Even in Madrid, ordinary Spaniards live in fear and poverty.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/20/books/review/20-BKS-SMITH/20-BKS-SMITH-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 466, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/20/books/review/20-BKS-SMITH/20-BKS-SMITH-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 700, 'width': 466, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/20/books/review/20-BKS-SMITH/20-BKS-SMITH-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/20/books/review/20-BKS-SMITH/20-BKS-SMITH-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/20/books/review/20-BKS-SMITH/20-BKS-SMITH-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In a Suspenseful New Novel From Ruta Sepetys, Franco-Era Spain Is as Repressive as Gilead', 'kicker': 'Children’s Books', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Novels', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Books and Literature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-09T14:37:33+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'BookReview', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sarah Harrison Smith', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sarah', 'middlename': 'Harrison', 'lastname': 'Smith', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3f4c0ec1-d83d-5954-8cd9-a3cd23bad781', 'word_count': 627, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3f4c0ec1-d83d-5954-8cd9-a3cd23bad781'}, {'abstract': 'Four years after his son’s fatal accident, the Australian musician has made an eerie, meditative album.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/09/arts/music/nick-cave-ghosteen-review.html', 'snippet': 'Four years after his son’s fatal accident, the Australian musician has made an eerie, meditative album.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some music sets out to conjure eternities. Extended drones, chantlike repeating phrases, tolling chords, spacious reverberation: Those are meditative sounds, defying fracture or interruption, tuning out the momentary and the trivial, invoking concentration, absorption, ritual and rapture. It’s the kind of music Nick Cave has chosen for “Ghosteen,” his 17th studio album leading the Bad Seeds.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/arts/09album-cave/merlin_162390537_eca3f318-ed92-4bd5-8384-380d0a01b9fe-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 398, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/10/arts/09album-cave/merlin_162390537_eca3f318-ed92-4bd5-8384-380d0a01b9fe-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 398}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/arts/09album-cave/merlin_162390537_eca3f318-ed92-4bd5-8384-380d0a01b9fe-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 679, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/arts/09album-cave/merlin_162390537_eca3f318-ed92-4bd5-8384-380d0a01b9fe-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1358, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name':