 added to its docket last week is flagrantly unconstitutional. My goal in this column is to make visible not only the stakes in the case but also Louisiana’s strategy for saving its law, the first of a wave of anti-abortion measures to reach a Supreme Court transformed by the retirement of Justice Anthony Kennedy and the addition of two justices appointed by President Donald Trump.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/opinion/10Greenhouse/10Greenhouse-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/10/opinion/10Greenhouse/10Greenhouse-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/opinion/10Greenhouse/10Greenhouse-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/opinion/10Greenhouse/10Greenhouse-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/opinion/10Greenhouse/10Greenhouse-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/10/opinion/10Greenhouse/10Greenhouse-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/opinion/10Greenhouse/10Greenhouse-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Supreme Court Abortion Case That Tests the Court Itself', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ABORTION', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Constitution (US)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Doctors', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Supreme Court (US)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Whole Woman's Health", 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ALITO, SAMUEL A JR', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Breyer, Stephen G', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'DeGravelles, John W (1948- )', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Scalia, Antonin', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kennedy, Anthony M', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kavanaugh, Brett M', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gorsuch, Neil M', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Louisiana', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Texas', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'United States', 'rank': 15, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-10T10:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Linda Greenhouse', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Linda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenhouse', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/0871aaa4-0063-5a25-a805-8b8fa30f3bfd', 'word_count': 1719, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0871aaa4-0063-5a25-a805-8b8fa30f3bfd'}, {'abstract': 'Violence against Jews is on the rise, but it doesn’t fit easily into the country’s polarized political climate.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/10/opinion/synagogue-attack-germany.html', 'snippet': 'Violence against Jews is on the rise, but it doesn’t fit easily into the country’s polarized political climate.', 'lead_paragraph': 'BERLIN — On Wednesday a gunman attacked a synagogue in the eastern German city of Halle while 51 Jews, including a group of young Americans, were inside observing Yom Kippur. When he found the door locked, he killed two people nearby and fled. The man filmed his assault and streamed it live on the internet. Journalists who have seen the video say that the man can be heard rambling anti-Semitic slurs. The police have arrested a suspect and confirmed that he is a 27-year-old German.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '27', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/opinion/10sauerbrey/merlin_162441987_24bd7d84-642e-4322-9f9e-78b0215013e0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/10/opinion/10sauerbrey/merlin_162441987_24bd7d84-642e-4322-9f9e-78b0215013e0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/opinion/10sauerbrey/merlin_162441987_24bd7d84-642e-4322-9f9e-78b0215013e0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/opinion/10sauerbrey/merlin_162441987_24bd7d84-642e-4322-9f9e-78b0215013e0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/opinion/10sauerbrey/merlin_162441987_24bd7d84-642e-4322-9f9e-78b0215013e0-thumbStand