'abstract': 'If it really does have to cut the power, it should be able to do so without giving California a panic attack.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/10/opinion/pg-and-e-power-shutdown.html', 'snippet': 'If it really does have to cut the power, it should be able to do so without giving California a panic attack.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Oakland, Calif. — There’s an unsettling quality to the weather during fire season in California, a frantic fluctuation from drizzle to blue skies to the dry gusty winds that transform small fires into big ones. It’s been a mild year so far. But in the wake of last year’s particularly destructive season the entire state seems to be bracing for disaster.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/opinion/10Lukas1/merlin_149224341_1b0d42c3-313e-4025-b661-5dce7afff1dc-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/10/opinion/10Lukas1/merlin_149224341_1b0d42c3-313e-4025-b661-5dce7afff1dc-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/opinion/10Lukas1/merlin_149224341_1b0d42c3-313e-4025-b661-5dce7afff1dc-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/opinion/10Lukas1/merlin_149224341_1b0d42c3-313e-4025-b661-5dce7afff1dc-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/opinion/10Lukas1/10Lukas1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/10/opinion/10Lukas1/10Lukas1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/opinion/10Lukas1/10Lukas1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Can’t PG&E Get It Together?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'California', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Pacific Gas and Electric Co', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wildfires', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Weather', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Power Failures and Blackouts', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Global Warming', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Forests and Forestry', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Weather Service', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Cal Fire', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-10T10:00:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michael David Lukas', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': 'David', 'lastname': 'Lukas', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/008e4663-b020-5a7b-837b-0fdc627a34e8', 'word_count': 1177, 'uri': 'nyt://article/008e4663-b020-5a7b-837b-0fdc627a34e8'}, {'abstract': 'Two ways that Democrats in the House can match the White House’s aggressive tactics.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/10/opinion/impeachment-contempt-congress.html', 'snippet': 'Two ways that Democrats in the House can match the White House’s aggressive tactics.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In his letter to House leadership, the White House counsel, Pat Cipollone, drew a line in the sand: The administration will not “participate in” the impeachment proceedings in any way. The odd language of “participate in” — presidential impeachment is not meant to be a collaboration between Congress and the president — obscures the central thrust of the letter: The White House is refusing to respond to any subpoenas or other demands for information from the House.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/09/opinion/10chafetz/merlin_161561043_a59f56f3-8cdf-4544-8706-0b2aff6abe24-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/09/opinion/10chafetz/merlin_161561043_a59f56f3-8cdf-4544-8706-0b2aff6abe24-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/09/opinion/10chafetz/merlin_161561043_a59f56f3-8cdf-4544-8706-0b2aff6abe24-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/09/opinion/10chafetz/merlin_161561043_a59f56f3-8cdf-4544-8706-0b2aff6abe24-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/09/opinion/10chafetz/merlin_161561043_a59f56f3-8cdf-4544-8706-0b2aff6abe24-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/0