anishes all too quickly from headlines, “Emanuel” offers a memorial. The documentary revisits the June 2015 killings at Emanuel African Methodist Episcopal Church in Charleston, S.C., by interviewing relatives of the victims, survivors of the shooting, journalists and public officials about their experiences of the crime or of first hearing about the deaths.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/arts/10emanuel-art/10emanuel-art-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 295, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/10/arts/10emanuel-art/10emanuel-art-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 295}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/arts/10emanuel-art/10emanuel-art-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 503, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/arts/10emanuel-art/10emanuel-art-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1006, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/arts/10emanuel-art/10emanuel-art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/10/arts/10emanuel-art/10emanuel-art-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/arts/10emanuel-art/10emanuel-art-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Emanuel’ Review: Race, Religion, Thoughts and Prayers', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Emanuel', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Documentary Films and Programs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Emanuel (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Ivie, Brian', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-10T11:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ben Kenigsberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ben', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenigsberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/8dc0ad7c-5226-5311-a459-722bdcdc94e7', 'word_count': 274, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8dc0ad7c-5226-5311-a459-722bdcdc94e7'}, {'abstract': 'Roger Avary’s new movie doesn’t add up to much more than scenes of breathtaking violence sprinkled with tasteless sexual humor.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/10/movies/lucky-day-review.html', 'snippet': 'Roger Avary’s new movie doesn’t add up to much more than scenes of breathtaking violence sprinkled with tasteless sexual humor.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Lucky Day,” directed by Roger Avary, begins in a prison cell, but rather than hearing from the bearded fellow in that cell, the voice-over is of a young girl. She’s Beatrice, daughter of prisoner Red, bemoaning the fact that her dad has missed two years of her growth.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/arts/10luckyday/merlin_162276276_cbfb8f06-472d-4a4f-915c-a91838ed5eca-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/10