: {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Patriots Wobble for a Bit, Then Demolish the Giants', 'kicker': 'Patriots 35, Giants 14', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pats Force 4 Turnovers From Jones In Blowout', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Football', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New York Giants', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'New England Patriots', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Brady, Tom', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Daniel (1997- )', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-11T04:26:44+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Pro Football', 'byline': {'original': 'By Bill Pennington', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Bill', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pennington', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f409f6d1-197a-5664-912d-2999d2f41428', 'word_count': 697, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f409f6d1-197a-5664-912d-2999d2f41428'}, {'abstract': 'A “Breaking Bad” movie hits Netflix. And Lupita Nyong’o eviscerates zombies on Hulu in “Little Monsters.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/11/arts/television/whats-on-tv-friday-el-camino-and-little-monsters.html', 'snippet': 'A “Breaking Bad” movie hits Netflix. And Lupita Nyong’o eviscerates zombies on Hulu in “Little Monsters.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'EL CAMINO: A BREAKING BAD MOVIE (2019) Stream on Netflix. Over the course of its five seasons, “Breaking Bad” transformed the character Jesse Pinkman from a dewy-eyed, small-time drug dealer into a hardened (if also penitent) desperado. The series began with Jesse (played by Aaron Paul) joining forces with Walter White (Bryan Cranston), a New Mexico high school chemistry teacher who starts cooking and distributing crystal meth to pay for cancer treatment. The last time we saw Jesse — after the drug empire the pair built together had collapsed — he was a scarred man speeding into the night behind the wheel of a stolen Chevrolet El Camino. This sequel, an epilogue of sorts from the series’s creator, Vince Gilligan, picks up the story from there. “It’s a chapter of ‘Breaking Bad’ that I didn’t realize that I wanted,” Paul said in a recent interview with The New York Times. “And now that I have it, I’m so happy that it’s there.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/11/arts/11tvcol-elcamino/11tvcol-elcamino-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/11/arts/11tvcol-elcamino/11tvcol-elcamino-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/11/arts/11tvcol-elcamino/11tvcol-elcamino-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/11/arts/11tvcol-elcamino/11tvcol-elcamino-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/11/arts/11tvcol-elcamino/11tvcol-elcamino-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/11/arts/11tvcol-elcamino/11tvcol-elcamino-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image',