com/2019/10/11/us/politics/2020-democrats-primary-polls.html', 'snippet': 'As next week’s debate looms, polls and donor contributions suggest a party seeking candidates who will push the boundaries, while moderates argue they can beat President Trump.', 'lead_paragraph': 'With a crucial debate looming next week in the Democratic presidential primary, the party’s populist wing appears increasingly in control of the race — rising in the polls, stocked with cash and with only a wounded leading candidate, Joseph R. Biden Jr., standing in its way.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/11/us/politics/11dems2020-01/merlin_162007722_15acd1d3-0966-4475-b21d-f7547324e8f5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/11/us/politics/11dems2020-01/merlin_162007722_15acd1d3-0966-4475-b21d-f7547324e8f5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/11/us/politics/11dems2020-01/merlin_162007722_15acd1d3-0966-4475-b21d-f7547324e8f5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/11/us/politics/11dems2020-01/merlin_162007722_15acd1d3-0966-4475-b21d-f7547324e8f5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/11/us/politics/11dems2020-01/11dems2020-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/11/us/politics/11dems2020-01/11dems2020-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/11/us/politics/11dems2020-01/11dems2020-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Populist Democrats Have Gained the Upper Hand in the 2020 Race', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Polling and Fund-Raising Suggest Populists Have the Upper Hand', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Debates (Political)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Biden, Joseph R Jr', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buttigieg, Pete (1982- )', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Bernard', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-11T09:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Politics', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexander Burns', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexander', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Burns', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/70f94da8-3e08-565e-afde-511510f972b4', 'word_count': 1641, 'uri': 'nyt://article/70f94da8-3e08-565e-afde-511510f972b4'}, {'abstract': 'Post-bloom, flowers become dried seed heads — and an entirely different kind of beautiful.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/11/t-magazine/winter-garden.html', 'snippet': 'Post-bloom, flowers become dried seed heads — and an entirely different kind of beautiful.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TO FLOWER, literally and figuratively, is to reach the peak of one’s possibility, from which there is no direction but down. Or so we have been taught: that lushness equals splendor, that when a blossom wilts and fails, the plant that bore it is finished, returned to drabness, spent of purpose. Spring is a pageant, winter a graveyard. What a shock, then, this past spring at the venerable Royal Horticultural Society’s Chelsea Flower Show in London, to see — amid the ravishment of color and swollen blooms — an array of seed heads, pale and close to pure sculpture, without a petal in sight. It was at once austere and flagrant, a rebuttal of cherished notions of what a garden should be. This, too, is beauty, it seemed to say: this diminishing, these skeletons that remain after the gaudy heyday of blossoms is past.', 'print_section': 'M2', 'print_page': '104', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/t-magazine/10tmag-seedheads/10tmag-seedheads-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/10/t-magazine/10tmag-seedheads/10tmag-seedheads-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/t-magazine/10tmag-seedheads/10tmag-seedheads-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/t-magazine/10tmag-seedheads/10tmag-seedheads-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/t-magazine/10tmag-seedheads/10tmag-seedheads-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/10/t-magazine/10tmag-seedheads/10tmag-seedheads-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/10/t-magazine/10tmag-seedheads/10tmag-seedheads-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Barren Charms of a Winter Garden', 'kicker': 'Making It', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'After the Fall', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Flowers and Plants', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Gardens and Gardening', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Seeds', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Design', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Chelsea Flower Show', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Kent (England)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-11T09:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'TStyle', 'section_name': 'T Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ligaya Mishan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ligaya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Mishan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/91f74afc-cbdd-5986-8b1e-e041c4778698', 'word_count': 990, 'uri': 'nyt://article/91f74afc-cbdd-5986-8b1e-e041c4778698'}, {'abstract': 'The average airline passenger leaves behind about three pounds of waste each flight. One British design firm has ideas to bring down that number.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/11/us/airline-cabin-waste.html', 'snippet': 'The average airline passenger leaves behind about three pounds of waste each flight. One British design firm has ideas to bring down that number.', 'lead_paragraph': 'From disposable headphones and plastic cutlery to food scraps and toilet waste, the average airline passenger leaves behind over three pounds of garbage, according to one estimate. To get travelers and airlines thinking — and talking — about that rather large pile of trash, a British design firm has refashioned the economy meal tray, replacing plastic with renewable materials such as coffee grounds, banana leaves and coconut wood.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/08/multimedia/00xp-airlinewaste5/00xp-airlinewaste5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/08/multimedia/00xp-airlinewaste5/00xp-airlinewaste5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/08/multimedia/00xp-airlinewaste5/00xp-airlinewaste5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/08/multimedia/00xp-airlinewaste5/00xp-airlinewaste5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/08/multimedia/00xp-airlinewaste5/00xp-airlinewaste5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/08/multimedia/00xp-airlinewaste5/00xp-airlinewaste5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/08/multimedia/00xp-airlinewaste5/00xp-airlinewaste5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Airline Food Waste Is a Problem. Can Banana Leaves Be Part of the Solution?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Can Banana Leaves Be Part of the Solution to Airline Waste?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Waste Materials and Disposal', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRLINES AND AIRPLANES', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fuel Emissions (Transportation)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'AIRPORTS', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Design Museum (London, England)', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-11T09:00:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Express', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': 'By Emily S. Rueb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Emily', 'middlename': 'S.', 'lastname': 'Rueb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a96595e8-804b-54c3-a968-98aecd6ffd7e', 'word_count': 1088, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a96595e8-804b-54c3-a968-98aecd6ffd7e'}, {'abstract': 'Unsteady glaciers pose dangers to Alpine towns and tourist areas; the challenge is letting people know when to get out of harm’s way.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/11/travel/alps-glaciers-climate-change.html', 'snippet': 'Unsteady glaciers pose dangers to Alpine towns and tourist areas; the challenge is letting people know when to get out of harm’s way.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For over a century, the Jungfrau Railway has delivered tourists high into the wild and frozen terrain of Switzerland’s Bernese Alps. In 2018, more than one million people rode the train up to the Jungfraujoch, a railway station — the highest in Europe — that occupies a rocky perch between the Jungfrau and the Mönch, two of the country’s most famous peaks. The train goes through a tunnel for much of the journey, but just before plunging into darkness, it passes below a small hanging glacier. Four years ago, scientists discovered that the glacier was at risk of collapse.', 'print_section': 'TR', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/11/travel/11alps/11alps-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 382, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/11/travel/11alps/11alps-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 382}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/11/travel/11alps/11alps-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 651, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/11/travel/11alps/11alps-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1303, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/11/travel/11alps/11alps-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/11/travel/11alps/11alps-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url