icholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bogel-Burroughs', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/69fae4ba-21b4-5e45-8196-2a874bbace78', 'word_count': 876, 'uri': 'nyt://article/69fae4ba-21b4-5e45-8196-2a874bbace78'}, {'abstract': 'Instagram-ready works of art and graphic design — sometimes whimsical, mostly anonymous — are defining features of the city’s antigovernment demonstrations.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/11/world/asia/hong-kong-protest-art.html', 'snippet': 'Instagram-ready works of art and graphic design — sometimes whimsical, mostly anonymous — are defining features of the city’s antigovernment demonstrations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HONG KONG — Soon after a woman in Hong Kong was hit in the eye at a protest, her likeness began circulating as a meme on internet forums where many demonstrators blamed her injury on the police. Within a couple of weeks, protesters had raised over $25,000 online to build a 13-foot statue of her.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/world/14hk-protest-art1/merlin_161643690_69d97566-2ec2-4fba-8d45-a0c1a0a84765-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/14/world/14hk-protest-art1/merlin_161643690_69d97566-2ec2-4fba-8d45-a0c1a0a84765-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/world/14hk-protest-art1/merlin_161643690_69d97566-2ec2-4fba-8d45-a0c1a0a84765-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 't