and to help displaced Syrians return home.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ANKARA, Turkey — It is dismaying that Turkey’s military operation in northeastern Syria is being spun in the American news media as an attack on Kurds, as weakening the fight against the remnants of Daesh (or the so-called Islamic State) and hurting America’s credibility with its allies. I am compelled to set the record straight because the 67-year-old NATO alliance that Turkey has with the United States is not temporary, tactical nor transactional. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/opinion/11Cavusoglu1/merlin_162487146_2c60e0ed-7426-4ca8-a76d-d8c6c2dcecec-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/14/opinion/11Cavusoglu1/merlin_162487146_2c60e0ed-7426-4ca8-a76d-d8c6c2dcecec-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/opinion/11Cavusoglu1/merlin_162487146_2c60e0ed-7426-4ca8-a76d-d8c6c2dcecec-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/opinion/11Cavusoglu1/merlin_162487146_2c60e0ed-7426-4ca8-a76d-d8c6c2dcecec-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/opinion/11Cavusoglu1/11Cavusoglu1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/14/opinion/11Cavusoglu1/11Cavusoglu1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}