terature', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-11T20:15:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Books', 'section_name': 'Books', 'subsection_name': 'Book Review', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/7ff1e9e7-77a3-56ac-a82c-e375f5f8aac4', 'word_count': 294, 'uri': 'nyt://article/7ff1e9e7-77a3-56ac-a82c-e375f5f8aac4'}, {'abstract': 'The organization said it was quickly running out of cash largely because a number of countries, chiefly the United States, have not paid all their annual assessments.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/11/world/americas/UN-cash-shortage.html', 'snippet': 'The organization said it was quickly running out of cash largely because a number of countries, chiefly the United States, have not paid all their annual assessments.', 'lead_paragraph': 'No new hiring, after-hours meetings or late-night receptions at the United Nations headquarters. No more optional travel. No new furniture or replacement computers unless absolutely necessary. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/11/world/11nations/merlin_161409231_f2a49252-98c1-4866-b7b0-f64f94dac5f4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/11/world/11nations/merlin_161409231_f2a49252-98c1-4866-b7b0-f64f94dac5f4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/11/world/11nations/merlin_161409231_f2a49252-98c1-4866-b7b0-f64f94dac5f4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'image