s.com/2019/10/11/sports/baseball/masaichi-kaneda-dead.html', 'snippet': 'A swaggering player with a quirky warm-up routine, he set pitching records for wins (400), strikeouts (4,490), innings (5,526⅔) — and losses (298).', 'lead_paragraph': 'Masaichi Kaneda started each of the thousands of innings he pitched during his illustrious career in Japan the same way. He walked to the mound, dropped his glove, grabbed the rosin bag, tossed it a few times, dropped it and then picked up his glove. Then he walked to second base, where he threw the first of eight warm-up pitches to the catcher. After each throw, he moved a few steps closer to the mound, until by the eighth pitch he was standing on the pitching rubber.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/12/obituaries/12Kaneda-obit/11Kaneda3-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 836, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/12/obituaries/12Kaneda-obit/11Kaneda3-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 836}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/12/obituaries/12Kaneda-obit/11Kaneda3-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 735, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/12/obituaries/12Kaneda-obit/11Kaneda3-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1470, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/12/obituaries/12Kaneda-obit/11Kaneda3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/12/obituaries/12Kaneda-obit/11Kaneda3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/12/obituaries/12Kaneda-obit/11Kaneda3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Masaichi Kaneda, Japan’s ‘Emperor’ of Baseball, Dies at 86', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Masaichi Kaneda, Pitcher, Who Set Record for Wins In Japan, Is Dead at 86', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'KANEDA, MASAICHI', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Japan', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-11T21:36:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ken Belson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ken', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Belson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/444b9841-8c81-5e5a-ad29-334f6726052b', 'word_count': 995, 'uri': 'nyt://article/444b9841-8c81-5e5a-ad29-334f6726052b'}, {'abstract': 'He received widespread attention for his dramatic protest against the Roman Catholic Church after it blocked the passage of a reproductive health bill.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/11/world/asia/carlos-celdran-dead.html', 'snippet': 'He received widespread attention for his dramatic protest against the Roman Catholic Church after it blocked the passage of a reproductive health bill.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Carlos Celdran, a Philippine cultural activist and performance artist who received national attention fo