motional Support Animals And a Co-op That Bans Large Dogs', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Real Estate and Housing (Residential)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pets', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Dogs', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-13T14:04:18+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'RealEstate', 'section_name': 'Real Estate', 'byline': {'original': 'By Ronda Kaysen', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Ronda', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kaysen', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/dd411309-3750-53e3-acb9-fa2c90eea1d2', 'word_count': 429, 'uri': 'nyt://article/dd411309-3750-53e3-acb9-fa2c90eea1d2'}, {'abstract': 'It may be the day to make a quick vegetable paella, chickpea harissa soup or miso chicken.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/13/dining/what-to-cook-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'It may be the day to make a quick vegetable paella, chickpea harissa soup or miso chicken.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Good morning. This might be the day to make Kay Chun’s recipe for vegetable paella with chorizo (above), but I’ve been cooking on a pellet grill recently, essentially a souped-up electric smoker that burns hardwood sawdust kibble, and it’s occupying all my thoughts. At low temperatures, it’s pretty cool, a machine that cooks ribs the way wave machines deliver three-footers to bodysurfing vacationers in Vegas: so reliably as to be kind of strange.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/19/dining/kc-smoky-paella-copy/merlin_150673158_d668aacc-20a3-455b-8138-cadd0f8aba5c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/0