ws_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Pavin Chachavalpongpun', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Pavin', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Chachavalpongpun', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/f2fee770-c4c1-5045-b0d3-393114803f7f', 'word_count': 1135, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f2fee770-c4c1-5045-b0d3-393114803f7f'}, {'abstract': 'The second season of the historical horror show wraps up. And Georges Franju’s tribute to early film serials arrives on the Criterion Channel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/14/arts/television/whats-on-tv-monday-the-finale-of-the-terror-infamy-and-franjus-judex.html', 'snippet': 'The second season of the historical horror show wraps up. And Georges Franju’s tribute to early film serials arrives on the Criterion Channel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'THE TERROR: INFAMY 9 p.m. on AMC. The dark side of history mingles with the supernatural in surprising and sometimes ambiguous ways in this anthology horror series. Season 2, which will conclude tonight, is particularly focused on the banal evil of politics and otherworldly malevolence. Set mostly in a Japanese internment camp during World War II, it follows Chester (Derek Mio) and his family in the aftermath of the Pearl Harbor attack. They are shadowed by Yuko (Kiki Sukezane), a mysterious being who has some designs on the child Chester’s wife, Luz (Cristina Rodlo), is carrying. Yuko, it turns out, is connected to Chester’s past. She is also a tormented shape-shifting spirit. The season’s penultimate episode resolved some of its central mysteries, including why Yuko wants Chester’s son, but it remains to be seen how Chester will try to vanquish her.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/arts/14tvcol-1/14tvcol-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/14/arts/14tvcol-1/14tvcol-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/arts/14tvcol-1/14tvcol-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/arts/14tvcol-1/14tvcol-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/arts/14tvcol-1/14tvcol-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/14/arts/14tvcol-1/14tvcol-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/arts/14tvcol-1/14tvcol-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Monday: The Finale of ‘The Terror: Infamy’ and Franju’s ‘Judex’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Monday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-14T05:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By Peter Libbey', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Peter', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Libbey', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/168298fa-82b5-51fa-9d47-17288c877747', 'word_count': 454, 'uri': 'nyt://article/168298fa-82b5-51fa-9d47-17288c877747'}, {'abstract': 'A decade after Congress gave the F.D.A. the power to regulate tobacco products like e-cigarettes, the federal government has repeatedly delayed or weakened efforts that could have protected teenagers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/14/health/vaping-e-cigarettes-fda.html', 'snippet': 'A decade after Congress gave the F.D.A. the power to regulate tobacco products like e-cigarettes, the federal government has repeatedly delayed or weakened efforts that could have protected teenagers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 2009, not long after Dr. Margaret Hamburg became commissioner of the Food and Drug Administration, a package arrived at her home. Inside was a clunky device called an e-cigarette.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/science/14VAPING-REG2/merlin_160778304_8ad9975a-c1ef-4ba7-8bf7-3569e736c5b2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/14/science/14VAPING-REG2/merlin_160778304_8ad9975a-c1ef-4ba7-8bf7-3569e736c5b2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/science/14VAPING-REG2/merlin_160778304_8ad9975a-c1ef-4ba7-8bf7-3569e736c5b2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/science/14VAPING-REG2/merlin_160778304_8ad9975a-c1ef-4ba7