nt_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Investigative', 'section_name': 'Business Day', 'byline': {'original': 'By Alexandra Stevenson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Alexandra', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Stevenson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/a4d4bdd5-33b5-554b-8c05-657a86174220', 'word_count': 1173, 'uri': 'nyt://article/a4d4bdd5-33b5-554b-8c05-657a86174220'}, {'abstract': 'Yotam Ottolenghi’s love of wine and cheese leads to a pie inspired by fondue parties from long ago.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/14/dining/fondue-pie-recipe.html', 'snippet': 'Yotam Ottolenghi’s love of wine and cheese leads to a pie inspired by fondue parties from long ago.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON —\xa0The combination of wine and cheese is one that I particularly cherish. Often, instead of dinner or as a bedtime snack, I see my day off with a glass of Chianti and chunk of Parmesan or mature pecorino. I am obviously not the first to discover the power couple that is wine and cheese, but it works particularly well for me because, after a day of testing recipes, all I want is to tickle my taste buds without overloading my stomach.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/11otto1/11otto1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/11otto1/11otto1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/11otto1/11otto1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/11otto1/11otto1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/11otto1/11otto1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/11otto1/11otto1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/11otto1/11otto1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Fondue Flavor, but Make It Pie', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Fondue Flavor, but Make It Pie', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cheese', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Squash (Vegetable)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pies', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-14T16:26:56+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Yotam Ottolenghi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Yotam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ottolenghi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/b29c60c3-acdd-5583-bcdb-02f4ec09d258', 'word_count': 687, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b29c60c3-acdd-5583-bcdb-02f4ec09d258'}, {'abstract': 'After a decade and a half of semi-fame, the writer and performer thought he had things figured out. Until he met two dogs more famous than he was.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/14/magazine/john-hodgman-medallion-status-excerpt.html', 'snippet': 'After a decade and a half of semi-fame, the writer and performer thought he had things figured out. Until he met two dogs more famous than he was.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The moment I stopped understanding how entertainment worked anymore happened when I was invited to a party in Adam Savage’s secret workshop. Adam Savage used to be a MythBuster on the show “MythBusters,” but his passion has always been prop replication. This means he would take his mythbusting money and funnel it into, say, building a perfect replica of the Maltese falcon from “The Maltese Falcon,” using the actual materials they would have used in 1941 to make actual Maltese falcons. I don’t know what those materials are. Vintage falcon malt, I guess. I don’t know. Ask him.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/magazine/14mag-hodgman-01/14mag-hodgman-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 338, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/14/magazine/14mag-hodgman-01/14mag-hodgman-01-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 338}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/magazine/14mag-hodgman-01/14mag-hodgman-01-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/magazine/14mag-hodgman-01/14mag-hodgman-01-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/magazine/14mag-hodgman-01/14mag-hodgman-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/14/magazine/14mag-hodgman-01/14mag-hodgman-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/magazine/14mag-hodgman-01/14mag-hodgman-01-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'John Hodgman on the Two Celebrity Corgis That Shattered His World', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Emmy Awards', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Daily Show with Jon Stewart (TV Program)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-14T16:30:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Hodgman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hodgman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f44b29b8-abc7-5cfd-ae15-27efbf609276', 'word_count': 3603, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f44b29b8-abc7-5cfd-ae15-27efbf609276'}, {'abstract': 'Scientists are trying to work out why some manta rays have black blotches on their skin, which is uncommon in the oceans.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/14/science/manta-rays-black.html', 'snippet': 'Scientists are trying to work out why some manta rays have black blotches on their skin, which is uncommon in the oceans.', 'lead_paragraph': "Spanning up to 25 feet from wing to wing, manta rays look like U.F.O.'s from below. If you ever get a chance to dive with them, look up. Lights won’t beam down and abduct you, but something about their bellies may surprise you. Most are white, but some are splattered with unique black blotches.", 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/22/science/00OBSTB-MANTARAYS/00TB-MANTARAYS-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/22/science/00OBSTB-MANTARAYS/00TB-MANTARAYS-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/22/science/00OBSTB-MANTARAYS/00TB-MANTARAYS-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/22/science/00OBSTB-MANTARAYS/00TB-MANTARAYS-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1281, 'width': 1920, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/22/science/00OBSTB-MANTARAYS/00TB-MANTARAYS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/22/science/00OBSTB-MANTARAYS/00TB-MANTARAYS-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/22/science/00OBSTB-MANTARAYS/00TB-MANTARAYS-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Mystery of the Melanistic Manta Rays', 'kicker': 'Trilobites', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Darkness Below: The Mysterious, Melanistic Manta Rays', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Stingrays', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Genetics and Heredity', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Color', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Fish and Other Marine Life', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Proceedings of the Royal Society B (Journal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indonesia', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Far East, South and Southeast Asia and Pacific Areas', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Pacific Ocean', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Indian Ocean', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-science', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-14T16:32:46+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By JoAnna Klein', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joanna', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Klein', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c71e0e8a-59ba-5bf3-a8fa-27b5bfb6554b', 'word_count': 597, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c71e0e8a-59ba-5bf3-a8fa-27b5bfb6554b'}, {'abstract': 'With a new “Addams Family” movie in theaters, a look back at the portrayal of one of its most popular family members over the years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/14/movies/wednesday-addams-family.html', 'snippet': 'With a new “Addams Family” movie in theaters, a look back at the portrayal of one of its most popular family members over the years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Twenty-six years after their last big-screen outing, the Addams Family is back in theaters. And yes, still creepy, kooky, mysterious and spooky (now also digitally animated). The family, created by the cartoonist Charles Addams, has been featured across magazines, films, television and a stage musical over the last 80 years, but no character has been portrayed quite as differently as the daughter, Wednesday — from a cherubic little girl in the 1960s to a stern and frightening adolescent in the 1990s to a lovesick teenager in the 2010s. Here’s a closer look at how Wednesday has been depicted in many variations by those writing, drawing and playing her. ', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/08/arts/addams-wednesday2/merlin_162281055_73efd670-d3e1-4bc2-be71-b60f7e3b921b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 316, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/08/arts/addams-wednesday2/merlin_162281055_73efd670-d3e1-4bc2-be71-b60f7e3b921b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 316}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/08/arts/addams-wednesday2/merlin_162281055_73efd670-d3e1-4bc2-be71-b60f7e3b921b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 540, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/08/arts/addams-wednesday2/merlin_162281055_73efd670-d3e1-4bc2-be71-b60f7e3b921b-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1080, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/08/arts/addams-wednesday2/addams-wednesday2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thum