ization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/434b8b6f-fc7f-5af1-91aa-f68db268bd7a', 'word_count': 372, 'uri': 'nyt://article/434b8b6f-fc7f-5af1-91aa-f68db268bd7a'}, {'abstract': 'Bigotry, both racial and religious, is the last refuge of a scoundrel.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/14/opinion/trump-william-barr-speech.html', 'snippet': 'Bigotry, both racial and religious, is the last refuge of a scoundrel.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Listening to the speech William Barr, the attorney general, gave last week at the University of Notre Dame Law School, I found myself thinking of the title of an old movie: “God Is My Co-Pilot.” What I realized is that Donald Trump’s minions have now gone that title one better: If Barr’s speech is any indication, their strategy is to make God their boss’s co-conspirator.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/opinion/14krugman1/14krugman1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 399, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/14/opinion/14krugman1/14krugman1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 399}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/opinion/14krugman1/14krugman1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 681, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/opinion/14krugman1/14krugman1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1363, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/opinion/14krugman1/14krugman1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/14/opinion/14krugman1/14krugman1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/14/opinion/14krugman1/14krugman1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'God Is Now Trump’s Co-Conspirator', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'God Is Now Trump’s Co-Conspirator', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Religion-State Relations', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Freedom of Religion', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Barr, William P', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-14T22:30:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Paul Krugman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Paul', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Krugman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/fd5fbffe-e5d8-5105-ba02-502f488cf31b', 'word_count': 884, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fd5fbffe-e5d8-5105-ba02-502f488cf31b'}, {'abstract': 'In his new cookbook, “Mixtape Potluck,” the musician shares recipes from some of his celebrity friends.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/14/dining/mixtape-potluck-questlove.html', 'snippet': 'In his new cookbook, “Mixtape Potluck,” the musician shares recipes from some of his celebrity friends.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The multifaceted career of Questlove (Ahmir Thompson), the musician and entertainer, includes food salons, where chefs cook for high-profile guests. With his new book “Mixtape Potluck,” he has turned things around and has guests do the cooking. Recipes, usually enough to feed a dozen or more, have been contributed by 57 of his friends. Zooey Deschanel’s bok choy and cucumber salad, JJ Johnson’s sticky ribs, Lilly Singh’s mother’s chicken curry, Eric Ripert’s salmon rillettes, Shep Gordon’s Maui onion and ginger soup, and Natalie Portman’s Greek spinach pie, using phyllo like a pie crust, are some worth serving. He has created a list of songs, inspired by the various contributors, for the cook to play while preparing each dish. Prince’s “Joint 2 Joint” is a suggestion for Ms. Deschanel. Questlove also shares party-hosting advice.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/14burner1/14burner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 793, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/14burner1/14burner1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 793}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/14burner1/14burner1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 776, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/14burner1/14burner1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1551, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/14burner1/14burner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/14burner1/14burner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/14burner1/14burner1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'You’re Invited to This Questlove Party', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Enjoy: You’re Invited To This Questlove Party', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Thompson, Ahmir (Questlove)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Mixtape Potluck (Book)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-14T22:31:28+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/eaea7650-2148-50c3-b70c-c61dfb77e3a3', 'word_count': 183, 'uri': 'nyt://article/eaea7650-2148-50c3-b70c-c61dfb77e3a3'}, {'abstract': 'The Wild World Fermentation Festival lands in Brooklyn with wines, ciders and beer from more than 50 producers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/14/dining/wild-world-fermentation-festival.html', 'snippet': 'The Wild World Fermentation Festival lands in Brooklyn with wines, ciders and beer from more than 50 producers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The trial run for Wild World Fermentation Festival, a natural wine fair, took place last spring in Austin, Texas. Success of the fair, which also featured wild-fermented ciders and beers, has led to a repeat in Brooklyn on Oct. 28. In addition to samples of wines, beers and ciders from more than 50 producers, there will be some fermented foods, talks and panel discussions.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/14burner5/merlin_162494097_8a6e0464-8127-4709-b336-90ac241c867e-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 337, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/14burner5/merlin_162494097_8a6e0464-8127-4709-b336-90ac241c867e-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 337}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/14burner5/merlin_162494097_8a6e0464-8127-4709-b336-90ac241c867e-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 576, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/14burner5/merlin_162494097_8a6e0464-8127-4709-b336-90ac241c867e-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1152, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/14burner5/14burner5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/14burner5/14burner5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/14burner5/14burner5-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Wild World of Natural Wine', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Sample: Fermentation Festival Heads to Brooklyn', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Berg'n (Brooklyn, NY, Restaurant)", 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Brooklyn (NYC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Beer', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cider', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-14T22:34:11+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d3026f38-9e7d-515e-9d05-a7aeaf42f5dd', 'word_count': 116, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d3026f38-9e7d-515e-9d05-a7aeaf42f5dd'}, {'abstract': 'These new oven mitts from the Metropolitan Museum of Art look like the armor of a 16th-century duke.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/14/dining/oven-mitt-armor.html', 'snippet': 'These new oven mitts from the Metropolitan Museum of Art look like the armor of a 16th-century duke.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Arm yourself as you light the grill, pull a sheet-pan dinner from the oven or baste the Thanksgiving turkey in its roasting pan with these amusing oven mitts. They’re printed with images of steel and gilded gauntlets of the 16th-century Duke of Saxe-Weimar, as displayed in the new exhibition “The Last Knight: The Art, Armor and Ambition of Maximilian I” at the Metropolitan Museum of Art.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/14burner4/merlin_162492183_bb2aeb63-2023-43