cle', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/abc4d536-b98e-55cf-b789-eec17ea65b92', 'word_count': 112, 'uri': 'nyt://article/abc4d536-b98e-55cf-b789-eec17ea65b92'}, {'abstract': 'After shuttering its garment district shop, the chocolate company has a sliver of a storefront uptown.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/14/dining/kees-chocolates-upper-west-side.html', 'snippet': 'After shuttering its garment district shop, the chocolate company has a sliver of a storefront uptown.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Kee Ling Tong, who started her chocolate company in SoHo in 2002, is now selling her treats from a sliver of a storefront on the Upper West Side. These include her lovely handmade bonbons; sleek dark and milk chocolate bars with flavorings like almonds, bergamot, jasmine and hibiscus; and nut-studded bark and macarons. She has closed her shop in the garment district, but she still has an outlet in the HSBC Bank at 452 Fifth Avenue (40th Street).', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/14burner6/merlin_162496554_ef656d30-c97c-441b-ae5f-dbcabf94158f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/14burner6/merlin_162496554_ef656d30-c97c-441b-ae5f-dbcabf94158f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/dining/14burner6/merlin_162496554_ef656d30-c97c-441b-ae5f-dbcabf94158f-jumbo.jpg', 'height