x on inherited money or property — unlike wealth or estate taxes — would be hard for even the fanciest accountants to shake.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/15/opinion/rich-kids-can-spare-some-of-their-inheritance.html', 'snippet': 'A tax on inherited money or property — unlike wealth or estate taxes — would be hard for even the fanciest accountants to shake.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In America, if you play by the rules, working to earn a living and saving to provide for the future, taxes take a piece of your earnings. If you win a state lottery, you owe tax. But if you get lucky in the lottery of life and land an inheritance, you owe no federal tax. That isn’t fair, is it? Extending the federal tax code to include inheritances would end that inequity. Inheritance taxes — regulated differently in the states that have them — are a levy paid by a person who inherits money or property of a person who has died.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/15/opinion/15Aaron/merlin_160596108_3029d5f5-04c6-4824-aa7c-33d943843408-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/15/opinion/15Aaron/merlin_160596108_3029d5f5-04c6-4824-aa7c-33d943843408-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/15/opinion/15Aaron/merlin_160596108_3029d5f5-04c6-4824-aa7c-33d943843408-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/15/opinion/15Aaron/merlin_160596108_3029d5f5-04c6-4824-aa7c-33d943843408-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/15/opinion/15Aaron/15Aaron-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/15/opinion/15Aaron/15Aaron-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/15/opinion/15Aaron/15Aaron-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Rich Kids Can Spare Some of Their Inheritance', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Inheritance and Estate Taxes', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Tax', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sanders, Bernard', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Warren, Elizabeth', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Income Inequality', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-15T15:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Henry Aaron', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Henry', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Aaron', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/09be29f9-7a4e-5cd3-967b-1323fd1a4277', 'word_count': 1072, 'uri': 'nyt://article/09be29f9-7a4e-5cd3-967b-1323fd1a4277'}, {'abstract': 'It’s similar to how we got to Medicare in the first place: the failure of private insurance.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/15/opinion/medicare-for-all-insurance.html', 'snippet': 'It’s similar to how we got to Medicare in the first place: the failure of private insurance.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Much to the dismay of single-payer advocates, our current health insurance system is likely to end with a whimper, not a bang. The average person simply prefers what we know versus the bureaucracy we fear.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/15/opinion/15silvers1/15silvers1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/15/opinion/15silvers1/15silvers1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/15/opinion/15silvers1/15silvers1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/15/opinion/15silvers1/15silvers1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/15/opinion/15silvers1/15silvers1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/15/opinion/15silvers1/15silvers1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/15/opinion/15silvers1/15silvers1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'This Is the Most Realistic Path to Medicare for All', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Health Insurance and Managed Care', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Medicare', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Patient Protection and Affordable Care Act (2010)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-15T15:00:08+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By J.B. Silvers', 'person': [{'firstname': 'J.', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3d35b9a2-db79-52be-bfc1-53557cd6bb3c', 'word_count': 875, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3d35b9a2-db79-52be-bfc1-53557cd6bb3c'}, {'abstract': 'Google’s Pixel 4 is the newest example of how computational photography is driving the future of phone cameras.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/15/technology/personaltech/google-pixel-photography.html', 'snippet': 'Google’s Pixel 4 is the newest example of how computational photography is driving the future of phone cameras.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Not too long ago, tech giants like Apple and Samsung raved about the number of megapixels they were cramming into smartphone cameras to make photos look clearer. Nowadays, all the handset makers are shifting focus to the algorithms, artificial intelligence and special sensors that are working together to make our photos look more impressive.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/15/business/15Techfix-print/15Techfix-print-articleLarge.gif', 'height': 360, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge