anagement of hospitals.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/15/us/politics/native-americans-health-care.html', 'snippet': 'After decades of enduring poor care from the government-run Indian Health Service, tribal groups are taking over management of hospitals.', 'lead_paragraph': 'RAPID CITY, S.D. — When 6-month-old James Ladeaux got his second upper respiratory infection in a month, the doctor at the Sioux San Indian Health Service Hospital reassured his mother, Robyn Black Lance, that it was only a cold.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '13', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/11/us/politics/11dc-indianhealth1-promo2/11dc-indianhealth1-promo-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 893, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/11/us/politics/11dc-indianhealth1-promo2/11dc-indianhealth1-promo-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 893}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/11/us/politics/11dc-indianhealth1-promo2/11dc-indianhealth1-promo-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 688, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/11/us/politics/11dc-indianhealth1-promo2/11dc-indianhealth1-promo-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1376, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/11/us/politics/11dc-indianhealth1-promo2/11dc-indianhealth1-promo-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/11/us/politics/11dc-indianhealth1-promo2/11dc-indianhealth1-