y, Mick', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Connolly, Gerald E (1950- )', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-15T16:31:03+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Nicholas Fandos, Kenneth P. Vogel and Michael D. Shear', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Nicholas', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fandos', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Kenneth', 'middlename': 'P.', 'lastname': 'Vogel', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}, {'firstname': 'Michael', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': '', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 3}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/0d3842f7-ec05-5b0a-9621-a0fa1741047b', 'word_count': 2044, 'uri': 'nyt://article/0d3842f7-ec05-5b0a-9621-a0fa1741047b'}, {'abstract': 'Jenna Fischer and Angela Kinsey reunite to rewatch every episode of “The Office” for a new podcast.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/15/arts/television/the-office-jenna-fischer-podcast.html', 'snippet': 'Jenna Fischer and Angela Kinsey reunite to rewatch every episode of “The Office” for a new podcast.', 'lead_paragraph': 'For a show that was never a ratings smash during its nine-year run, “The Office” has experienced an astronomical afterlife. In fact, it had a second season thanks only to an NBC executive staking his reputation on its potential. But “The Office” — a drabby workplace sitcom that debuted in 2005 and was adapted from Ricky Gervais’s crueler British mockumentary series — has become Netflix’s most-watched show. It clocked 45.8 billion viewing minutes last year, according to Nielsen. That’s 14 billion more minutes than “Friends” garnered over that time, and 18.2 billion more than Netflix’s own hit “Stranger Things.”', 'print_sect