 '2019-10-16T14:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Arts&Leisure', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By A.O. Scott', 'person': [{'firstname': 'A.', 'middlename': 'O.', 'lastname': 'Scott', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/fe661900-9f5d-5064-8228-530aa53b3476', 'word_count': 1776, 'uri': 'nyt://article/fe661900-9f5d-5064-8228-530aa53b3476'}, {'abstract': 'The legendary stage actress’s character was shaped as much by the roles she lost as those she won. These are some of the ones that got away.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/16/theater/elaine-stritch-broadway-roles.html', 'snippet': 'The legendary stage actress’s character was shaped as much by the roles she lost as those she won. These are some of the ones that got away.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The performer Elaine Stritch died in 2014 at 89 after over 70 years appearing in plays, musicals, film, television, cabaret and newspaper gossip columns, telegrams and Twitter, saloons and recovery meetings. Throughout a marathon career, she came to define herself — acerbically, sometimes world-wearily, always energetically — as much by the roles she didn’t get (or was fired from) as her successes. ', 'print_section': 'AR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/20/arts/20stritch5/20stritch-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/20/arts/20stritch5/20stritch-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 425}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/20/arts/20stritch5/20stritch-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 726, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo',