e.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/opinion/16Boylan/16Boylan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 773, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/16/opinion/16Boylan/16Boylan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 773}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/opinion/16Boylan/16Boylan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 795, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/opinion/16Boylan/16Boylan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1589, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/opinion/16Boylan/16Boylan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/16/opinion/16Boylan/16Boylan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/opinion/16Boylan/16Boylan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Genius Behind the Grateful Dead', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Grateful Dead', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Garcia, Jerry', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Hunter, Robert C (1941- )', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-16T15:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Finney Boylan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': 'Finney', 'lastname': 'Boylan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/cab0804a-3f87-5c72-941a-dab1d607e280', 'word_count': 804, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cab0804a-3f87-5c72-941a-dab1d607e280'}, {'abstract': 'There are no formal rules for what is ethical — or even legal — in the location data business. That needs to change.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/16/opinion/foursquare-privacy-internet.html', 'snippet': 'There are no formal rules for what is ethical — or even legal — in the location data business. That needs to change.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the right hands, location data can be a force for good. It can provide publishers and app developers with advertising revenue so consumers can access free services and information. It can inform city planning, help ride-sharing users reach their destinations, guide travelers to great local spots, reassure parents their children are safely on their way home, remind people where they parked their car and relieve traffic congestion. And it has immense potential for the future: in autonomous driving, augmented reality, smarter health care interventions and context-aware artificial intelligence.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/opinion/16glueck-privacy/16glueck-privacy-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 450, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/16/opinion/16glueck-privacy/16glueck-privacy-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 450}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/opinion/16glueck-privacy/16glueck-privacy-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 768, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/opinion/16glueck-privacy/16glueck-privacy-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1536, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/opinion/16glueck-privacy/16glueck-privacy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/16/opinion/16glueck-privacy/16glueck-privacy-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/opinion/16glueck-privacy/16glueck-privacy-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Stop the Abuse of Location Data', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Data-Mining and Database Marketing', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Consumer Protection', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Privacy', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Law and Legislation', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Regulation and Deregulation of Industry', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Computers and the Internet', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Foursquare', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-16T15:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jeff Glueck', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jeff', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Glueck', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/c97071f1-b3eb-5551-81ec-d87e67052a35', 'word_count': 1425, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c97071f1-b3eb-5551-81ec-d87e67052a35'}, {'abstract': 'The United States and Europe are erroneously banking on sanctioning Turkey to contain the fallout in Syria.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/16/opinion/syria-turkey.html', 'snippet': 'The United States and Europe are erroneously banking on sanctioning Turkey to contain the fallout in Syria.', 'lead_paragraph': 'ISTANBUL — The sudden decision by President Trump to endorse Turkey’s move to send its troops into Syria and pull out most of the American forces posted there seems to have shocked the country’s political and military establishment. American analysts and policymakers see events of the past week as largely benefiting Russia, the Syrian government, the remnants of the Islamic State and Iran. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/opinion/16ulgen/16ulgen-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/16/opinion/16ulgen/16ulgen-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/opinion/16ulgen/16ulgen-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 682, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/opinion/16ulgen/16ulgen-superJumbo.jpg', 'height