 'article', 'news_desk': 'Society', 'section_name': 'Fashion & Style', 'subsection_name': 'Weddings', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2555209-2b5b-50e2-b5b3-e1d5228fc0b1', 'word_count': 266, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2555209-2b5b-50e2-b5b3-e1d5228fc0b1'}, {'abstract': 'Holding internet platforms liable for certain content would harm internet users.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/16/opinion/section-230-freedom-speech.html', 'snippet': 'Holding internet platforms liable for certain content would harm internet users.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Who benefits from Section 230, the federal law that shields online platforms from liability for content posted by users? According to commentators and politicians, Section 230 helps only large tech companies. But the biggest beneficiaries of Section 230 are internet users, not internet companies. Before Congress undermines Section 230, it must understand how users rely on it — and how the internet would change without it.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/opinion/16Harmon/merlin_154193565_919652cb-4c5b-42c6-b62a-afe946ae81c7-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/16/opinion/16Harmon/merlin_154193565_919652cb-4c5b-42c6-b62a-afe946ae81c7-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/opinion/16Harmon/merlin_154193565_919652cb-4c5b-42c6-b62a-afe946ae81c7-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/16/opini