s store Mjölk are discovering a slower lifestyle north of Lake Ontario.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A large, weathered copper planter sits between the open kitchen and the living room of John Baker and Juli Daoust’s country home, just north of the beaches and vineyards of Ontario, in Canada’s Prince Edward County. It is the kind of object you would expect to find at Mjölk, the husband-and-wife duo’s 10-year-old boutique and gallery in Toronto. This particular vessel happens to house a dead olive tree. “It’s an antique Japanese container, an industrial vat,” Baker told me. “This was alive,” he continued, referring to the brittle tree. “It didn’t survive — and that’s O.K.”', 'print_section': 'ST', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/23/t-magazine/23tmag-mjolk-slide-MOOZ/23tmag-mjolk-slide-MOOZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/09/23/t-magazine/23tmag-mjolk-slide-MOOZ/23tmag-mjolk-slide-MOOZ-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/23/t-magazine/23tmag-mjolk-slide-MOOZ/23tmag-mjolk-slide-MOOZ-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/23/t-magazine/23tmag-mjolk-slide-MOOZ/23tmag-mjolk-slide-MOOZ-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/09/23/t-magazine/23tmag-mjolk-slide-MOOZ/23tmag-mjolk-slide-MOOZ-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': '