ce and Ethnicity', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comic Books and Strips', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gossett, Lou Jr', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Chau, Hong (Actor)', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Gibbons, Dave', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Irons, Jeremy', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kassell, Nicole', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Lindelof, Damon', 'rank': 12, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Nelson, Tim Blake', 'rank': 13, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Redford, Robert', 'rank': 14, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-17T15:42:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Television', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Poniewozik', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Poniewozik', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/cb1f4458-574c-53d5-986d-4684fe5b2ef0', 'word_count': 1196, 'uri': 'nyt://article/cb1f4458-574c-53d5-986d-4684fe5b2ef0'}, {'abstract': 'America’s dual faith in individual liberty and democracy is under attack by the president’s populism.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/17/opinion/liberalism-trump.html', 'snippet': 'America’s dual faith in individual liberty and democracy is under attack by the president’s populism.', 'lead_paragraph': 'As the author of a recent book titled “What Was Liberalism?,” I have been chided by critics for joining a chorus of doomsayers. The stock of liberalism certainly looked low in 2016, when I began my research: Donald Trump was elected president and the British decided to leave the European Union. But Mr. Trump’s approval ratings have never climbed above the mid-40s, while the British seem to be regretting their rash decision. The popularity of nativist and reactionary parties in Europe has receded from its high-water mark of two or three years ago. So many liberal Democrats have decided to run against Mr. Trump that they can’t fit in one room. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/19/opinion/17Traub1/merlin_162789957_55428ef5-3747-4ce5-be5b-c4ec730a2037-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 392, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/19/opinion/17Traub1/merlin_162789957_55428ef5-3747-4ce5-be5b-c4ec730a2037-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 392}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/19/opinion/17Traub1/merlin_162789957_55428ef5-3747-4ce5-be5b-c4ec730a2037-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 669, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/19/opinion/17Traub1/merlin_162789957_55428ef5-3747-4ce5-be5b-c4ec730a2037-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1338, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/19/opinion/17Traub1/17Traub1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/19/opinion/17Traub1/17Traub1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/19/opinion/17Traub1/17Traub1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 