//article/7ebe02ab-70de-521a-a691-0f0f04508e4f'}, {'abstract': 'We didn’t die.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/18/opinion/sunday/gender-transition-death-grief.html', 'snippet': 'We didn’t die.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Shortly before my gender assignment surgery in 2002, my father told me that he was grieving the loss of his first-born son. My first impulse was to comfort him. We talked about his feelings one afternoon and I reassured him that he wasn’t losing me. I thought this was my duty; after all, he had supported my transition, defending me against bigoted relatives (even as he stumbled over my pronouns and told me I needed to be less argumentative if I planned to live as a woman).', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '10', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/20/opinion/sunday/20talusan/20talusan-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/20/opinion/sunday/20talusan/20talusan-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/20/opinion/sunday/20talusan/20talusan-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/20/opinion/sunday/20talusan/20talusan-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1800, 'width': 1800, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/20/opinion/sunday/20talusan/20talusan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/20/opinion/sunday/20talusan/20talusan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/20/opinion/sunday/20talusan/20talusan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Celebrate Your Kid’s Transition. Don’t Grieve It.', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'I Wish My Dad Had Celebrated My Transition', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Transgender and Transsexuals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Families and Family Life', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Parenting', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Philippines', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-18T15:22:20+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'subsection_name': 'Sunday Review', 'byline': {'original': 'By Meredith Talusan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Meredith', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Talusan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/3dce22d4-fd9a-51d9-9fb8-9778accc01e4', 'word_count': 905, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3dce22d4-fd9a-51d9-9fb8-9778accc01e4'}, {'abstract': 'If he acted “presidential,” Mr. Trump said Thursday night in Dallas, “everybody would be out of here so fast.”', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/18/us/politics/trump-presidency.html', 'snippet': 'If he acted “presidential,” Mr. Trump said Thursday night in Dallas, “everybody would be out of here so fast.”', 'lead_paragraph': 'DALLAS — At one point during one of his most unpresidential of days, President Trump insisted that he knew how to be presidential.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times',