anization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9bbae849-7b88-5f2b-9181-7e65f9e92c9f', 'word_count': 2063, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9bbae849-7b88-5f2b-9181-7e65f9e92c9f'}, {'abstract': 'A Times reporter says it is time to hold him accountable for his errant N.B.A. takes. Carmelo Anthony for Sixth Man of the Year?', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/18/sports/bad-nba-predictions.html', 'snippet': 'A Times reporter says it is time to hold him accountable for his errant N.B.A. takes. Carmelo Anthony for Sixth Man of the Year?', 'lead_paragraph': 'I am known around the office for bad takes. Or, rather, my co-workers claim that I have bad takes. Maybe it’s the Dave Matthews Band fan in me. Maybe it’s my affection for “Everybody Loves Raymond.” Or maybe it’s because I believe that the retired power forward Antoine Walker would easily be a top-10 player today.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/19/sports/19nba-badpredictions1-print/merlin_147060900_059b193e-02e0-47fb-be98-9fff927af4b4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/19/sports/19nba-badpredictions1-print/merlin_147060900_059b193e-02e0-47fb-be98-9fff927af4b4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/19/sports/19nba-badpredictions1-print/merlin_147060900_059b193e-02e0-47fb-be98-9fff927af4b4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/19/sports/19nba-badpredictions1-print/merlin_147060900_059b193e-02e0-47fb-be98-9fff927af4b4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/19/sports/19nba-badpredictions1-print/19nba-badpredictions-lede-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/19/sports/19nba-badpredictions1-print/19nba-badpredictions-lede-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/19/sports/19nba-badpredictions1-print/19nba-badpredictions-lede-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Look Back at One Reporter’s Bad N.B.A. Predictions', 'kicker': 'on pro basketball', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'This Crystal Ball Was at Times Clear But Had Its Cracks', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Basketball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'National Basketball Assn', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'ANTHONY, CARMELO', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-18T21:13:51+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sopan Deb', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sopan', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Deb', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9851126c-7349-55ef-ada9-8987d8d87eb8', 'word_count': 879, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9851126c-7349-55ef-ada9-8987d8d87eb8'}, {'abstract': 'After a forced sterilization at 19, she became first a sculptor and then an advocate for more humane psychiatric care in modern Germany and beyond.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/18/health/dorothea-buck-dead.html', 'snippet': 'After a forced sterilization at 19, she became first a sculptor and then an advocate for more humane psychiatric care in modern Germany and beyond.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In March 1936, a week before Hitler’s troops reoccupied the Rhineland, violating the treaty that a defeated Germany had signed to end World War I, Dorothea Buck, the 19-year-old daughter of a German pastor, was so traumatized by the prospect of another brutal European war that she had to be hospitalized.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/22/obituaries/22Buck-obit1/merlin_162809808_91e68834-2198-41de-a264-5dd0b6f267fd-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 901, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/22/obituaries/22Buck-obit1/merlin_162809808_91e68834-2198-41de-a264-5dd0b6f267fd-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 901}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/22/obituaries/22Buck-obit1/merlin_162809808_91e68834-2198-41de-a264-5dd0b6f267fd-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 682, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/22/obituaries/22Buck-obit1/merlin_162809808_91e68834-2198-41de-a264-5dd0b6f267fd-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1280, 'width': 852, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/22/obituaries/22Buck-obit1/16Buck2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/22/obituaries/22Buck-obit1/16Buck2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/22/obituaries/22Buck-obit1/16Buck2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Dorothea Buck, 102, Dies; Nazi Victim and Voice for Mentally Ill', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Dorothea Buck, 102, Advocate for Mental Patients, Dies', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Buck, Dorothea', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Deaths (Obituaries)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Holocaust and the Nazi Era', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mental Health and Disorders', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Psychiatry and Psychiatrists', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World War II (1939-45)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Sculpture', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Germany', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-18T21:14:34+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Obits', 'section_name': 'Health', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/e715bf6a-8227-532b-b840-6e9d7aadb1f6', 'word_count': 944, 'uri': 'nyt://article/e715bf6a-8227-532b-b840-6e9d7aadb1f6'}, {'abstract': 'One of them, Jason Reynolds’s middle-grade novel “Look Both Ways,” is a National Book Award finalist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/18/books/review/jason-reynolds-look-both-ways.html', 'snippet': 'One of them, Jason Reynolds’s middle-grade novel “Look Both Ways,” is a National Book Award finalist.', 'lead_paragraph': 'It’s fall, which means the best-seller lists are brimming with new titles — this week, 12 of them, including “The Giver of Stars,” Jojo Moyes’s novel about Depression-era librarians in Kentucky; “Deep State,” James Stewart’s look at how the F.B.I. investigated Hillary Clinton and Donald Trump; “Tough Love,” Susan Rice’s memoir about her life and her time as national security adviser; and “Ninth House,” Leigh Bardugo’s first adult novel, about a young woman deeply enmeshed in Yale’s secret societies. “Y.A. fiction tends to have a finite quality,” Bardugo told The Times recently. “You’re looking toward a goal — prom or graduation or revolution — and we leave these characters after a moment of tremendous transformation.” But in “Ninth House,” which is the first in a series, “the challenges faced by my heroine are different and don’t stop at one particular point,” she said.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '28', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/27/books/review/27insidethelist-web/27insidethelist-print-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/27/books/review/27insidethelist-web/27insidethelist-print-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/27/books/review/27insidethelist-web/27insidethelist-print-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/27/books/review/27insidethelist-web/27insidethelist-print-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo