 (Washington, DC)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cummings, Elijah E', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Funerals and Memorials', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-19T00:04:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sheryl Gay Stolberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sheryl', 'middlename': 'Gay', 'lastname': 'Stolberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/63de5f81-2685-52e1-aa26-2b2cdb84a288', 'word_count': 459, 'uri': 'nyt://article/63de5f81-2685-52e1-aa26-2b2cdb84a288'}, {'abstract': 'Kurds always get shafted. Still, this was American perfidy.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/18/opinion/trump-kurds-syria.html', 'snippet': 'Kurds always get shafted. Still, this was American perfidy.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — President Trump has given a master class in the unhappy link between his “gut” and the gutting of American credibility. His flippancy over the fate of the Kurds in northern Syria has been criminal in its disregard for human life, America’s friends and American interests. From Trump’s sort-of green light to Turkey’s assault on northern Syria, to his threat to “totally destroy and obliterate” the Turkish economy, to his Chamberlain-like dismissal of Kurds’ fate (“We are 7,000 miles away!”), he has played the clown in chief.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '22', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/21/opinion/18cohenWeb/merlin_162552252_8baa887f-8189-4e2f-af04-d243ac2bed58-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/21/opinion/18cohenWeb/merlin_162552252_8baa887f-8189-4e2f-af04-d243ac2bed58-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/21/opinion/18cohenWeb/merlin_162552252_8baa887f-8189-4e2f-af04-d243ac2bed58-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/21/opinion/18cohenWeb/merlin_162552252_8baa887f-8189-4e2f-af04-d243ac2bed58-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/21/opinion/18cohenWeb/18cohenWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/21/opinion/18cohenWeb/18cohenWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/21/opinion/18cohenWeb/18cohenWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump’s Gut, and the Gutting of American Credibility', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trump’s Gut, and the Gutting of American Credibility', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Syria', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Kurds', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Turkey', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States International Relations', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (