alifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Neil', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Vigdor', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Obituary (Obit)', '_id': 'nyt://article/48a99bbf-a30e-558f-a120-b53288d1eae7', 'word_count': 1150, 'uri': 'nyt://article/48a99bbf-a30e-558f-a120-b53288d1eae7'}, {'abstract': 'An incredible story of amnesia and family trauma hits Netflix, and the tale of Patsy Cline and Loretta Lynn’s friendship airs on Lifetime.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/19/arts/television/whats-on-tv-saturday-tell-me-who-i-am-and-patsy-loretta.html', 'snippet': 'An incredible story of amnesia and family trauma hits Netflix, and the tale of Patsy Cline and Loretta Lynn’s friendship airs on Lifetime.', 'lead_paragraph': 'TELL ME WHO I AM Stream on Netflix. At age 18, Alex Lewis woke up from a weeklong coma to discover that he had survived a devastating motorcycle accident, but lost most of his memory. At the hospital, he realizes he can’t remember who he is, how to walk or anything about his past — but he recognizes his identical twin brother, Marcus. This documentary follows the story of Alex’s recovery with Marcus as his guide, filling him in on the details of his childhood. But roughly a decade later, after the twins’ mother dies, Alex starts to question whether the childhood Marcus reconstructed for him was truthful, going on to uncover childhood trauma that he and his brother experienced before the accident. In his review for The New York Times, Glenn Kenny wrote that although the brothers recounted their story in a 2013 memoir, the film “functions as a continuation of the book, and ends in a staggering sequence in which Marcus is finally able to relay the whole truth to his brother.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '8', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/19/arts/19tvcol-tellme/19tvcol-tellme-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/19/arts/19tvcol-tellme/19tvcol-tellme-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/19/arts/19tvcol-tellme/19tvcol-tellme-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/19/arts/19tvcol-tellme/19tvcol-tellme-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/19/arts/19tvcol-tellme/19tvcol-tellme-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/19/arts/19tvcol-tellme/19tvcol-tellme-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/19/arts/19tvcol-tellme/19tvcol-tellme-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'What’s on TV Saturday: ‘Tell Me Who I Am’ and ‘Patsy & Loretta’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'What’s On Saturday', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Television', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-19T05:00:06+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Culture', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name':