 with progressive parties.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Justin Trudeau’s victory in Canada’s national elections on Monday followed what he called one of the “nastiest” campaigns in Canadian history. That may be true, to the degree that much of the campaign was about him and some bad decisions he made, and it featured a lot of name-calling. At one point supporters of his Conservative challenger even chanted “Lock him up, lock him up.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '26', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/22/opinion/22trudeauWeb/22trudeauWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 610, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/22/opinion/22trudeauWeb/22trudeauWeb-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 610}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/22/opinion/22trudeauWeb/22trudeauWeb-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1008, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/22/opinion/22trudeauWeb/22trudeauWeb-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2015, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/22/opinion/22trudeauWeb/22trudeauWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/22/opinion/22trudeauWeb/22trudeauWeb-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/22/opinion/22trudeauWeb/22trudeauWeb-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'th