mance, personalized medicine and whether and why people can respond so differently to the same exercise.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/well/physed-movement3/merlin_74227411_1cc233ae-1253-4fe2-948a-7603b68e79d0-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 261, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/29/well/physed-movement3/merlin_74227411_1cc233ae-1253-4fe2-948a-7603b68e79d0-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 261}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/well/physed-movement3/merlin_74227411_1cc233ae-1253-4fe2-948a-7603b68e79d0-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 445, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/well/physed-movement3/merlin_74227411_1cc233ae-1253-4fe2-948a-7603b68e79d0-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 891, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/well/physed-movement3/physed-movement3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/29/well/physed-movement3/physed-movement3-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/well/physed-movement3/physed-movement3-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Something in the Way We Move', 'kicker': 'Phys Ed', 'content_kicker': Non