3'}, {'abstract': 'On her debut album, “Cheap Queen,” 20-year-old Mikaela Straus crafts candid songs grounded — but not stuck — in past generations’ pop.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/23/arts/music/king-princess-cheap-queen-review.html', 'snippet': 'On her debut album, “Cheap Queen,” 20-year-old Mikaela Straus crafts candid songs grounded — but not stuck — in past generations’ pop.', 'lead_paragraph': 'King Princess — the songwriter Mikaela Straus, now 20 — launched her recording career early last year with “1950,” a streaming hit that begins with a blunt statement about her sexual orientation: “I hate it when dudes try to chase me.” Then it delves into an infatuation — “tell me why my gods look like you” — while imagining the repressed 1950s, when homosexuality was expected to stay closeted. ', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '6', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/23/arts/23album-kingprincess2/23album-kingprincess2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/23/arts/23album-kingprincess2/23album-kingprincess2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/23/arts/23album-kingprincess2/23album-kingprincess2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/23/arts/23album-kingprincess2/23album-kingprincess2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/23/arts/23album-kingprincess2/23album-ki