4/movies/the-great-alaskan-race-review.html', 'snippet': 'Brian Presley’s film squanders the dramatic ingredients of the early-20th-century sledding adventure it’s based on.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In 1925 a diphtheria outbreak in Nome, Alaska, led to what became a legendary sled race for lifesaving serum. For five and a half days in the dead of winter, a team of mushers and their dogs rushed from Nome and back, covering hundreds of miles to deliver medicine to the beleaguered, icebound city. The historic serum run combined dogs, sports and life-or-death stakes, a seemingly perfect setup for cinematic adaptation that “The Great Alaskan Race” fumbles.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '9', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/24/arts/24greatalaskan/merlin_162979956_8c76ce2c-2d96-41d5-81b5-6181aaf1a279-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 283, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/24/arts/24greatalaskan/merlin_162979956_8c76ce2c-2d96-41d5-81b5-6181aaf1a279-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 283}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/24/arts/24greatalaskan/merlin_162979956_8c76ce2c-2d96-41d5-81b5-6181aaf1a279-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 483, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/24/arts/24greatalaskan/merlin_162979956_8c76ce2c-2d96-41d5-81b5-6181aaf1a279-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 966, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/24/arts/24greatalaskan/24greatalaskan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/24/arts/24greatalaskan/24greatalaskan-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/24/arts/24greatalaskan/24greatalaskan-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘The Great Alaskan Race’ Review: A Historic Sled Rescue Turned to Mush', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'The Great  Alaskan Race', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'The Great Alaskan Race (Movie)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Presley, Brian (1977- )', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-24T11:00:07+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Teo Bugbee', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Teo', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Bugbee', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/10d419ec-7b16-5dc7-9970-6542ff819468', 'word_count': 277, 'uri': 'nyt://article/10d419ec-7b16-5dc7-9970-6542ff819468'}, {'abstract': 'The director Phillip Youmans completed this, his first feature, while still in his teens. It feels like the work of an older, and fully formed, artist.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/24/movies/burning-cane-review.html', 'snippet': 'The director Phillip Youmans completed this, his first feature, while still in his teens. It feels like the work of an older, and fully formed, artist.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Reflections From Damaged Life” was the subtitle the philosopher Theodor Adorno gave his book “Minima Moralia.” It is an apt description, too, of “Burning Cane,” the debut feature from a young filmmaker, Phillip Youmans. The movie begins with a voice-over from one of its central characters, Helen Wayne, describing in excruciating detail her beloved dog’s mange, and the seemingly dozens of ineffectual cures she has tried on it.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/25/arts/24burning/merlin_162979698_0fef3cbf-1f57-4374-a5d4-8da952532c16-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 324, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/25/arts/24burning/merlin_162979698_0fef3cbf-1f57-4374-a5d4-8da952532c16-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 324}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/25/arts/24burning/merlin_162979698_0fef3cbf-1f57-4374-a5d4-8da952532c16-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 554, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/25/arts/24burning/merlin_162979698_0fef3cbf-1f57-4374-a5d4-8da952532c16-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1107, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/25/arts/24burning/merlin_162979698_0fef3cbf-1f57-4374-a5d4-8da952532c16-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/25/arts/24burning/merlin_162979698_0fef3cbf-1f57-4374-a5d4-8da952532c16-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/25/arts/24burning/merlin_162979698_0fef3cbf-1f57-4374-a5d4-8da952532c16-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '‘Burning Cane’ Review: Poverty and Despair in Rural Louisiana', 'kicker': 'Critic’s Pick', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'A Constant Ache Shall Guide Them', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Movies', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Youmans, Phillip (Film Director)', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pierce, Wendell', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Burning Cane (Movie)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-24T11:00:10+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Movies', 'byline': {'original': 'By Glenn Kenny', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Glenn', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Kenny', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Review', '_id': 'nyt://article/3cea8289-342b-56c4-95d1-1ef6cba51855', 'word_count': 527, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3cea8289-342b-56c4-95d1-1ef6cba51855'}, {'abstract': 'Obesity is a population-size crisis in Western countries — but it’s a problem that may resist population-wide solutions.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/24/magazine/why-isnt-there-a-diet-that-works-for-everyone.html', 'snippet': 'Obesity is a population-size crisis in Western countries — but it’s a problem that may resist population-wide solutions.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the United States and other Western countries, diet and nutrition researchers face an urgent imperative: Figure out how to solve the crisis of obesity. About 40 percent of the adults and 19 percent of the children and adolescents in the United States have obesity, according to the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention. More and more of them face the increased risks of suffering from diabetes, cardiovascular disease and countless other negative health effects. This situation looks like a single problem from a population standpoint — one that simple guidelines for balancing calorie consumption and expenditure should be able to solve. Instead, a seeming infinitude of variables influence what each of us eats and how the body responds.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/27/magazine/27StudiesShow_small/27StudiesShow_small-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 592, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/27/magazine/27StudiesShow_small/27StudiesShow_small-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 592}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/27/magazine/27StudiesShow_small/27StudiesShow_small-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1011, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/27/magazine/27StudiesShow_small/27StudiesShow_small-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1908, 'width': 1933, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/27/magazine/27StudiesShow_small/27StudiesShow_small-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/27/magazine/27StudiesShow_small/27StudiesShow_small-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/27/magazine/27StudiesShow_small/27StudiesShow