rab breaks into a skipping run, throwing itself on the treat with abandon.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/science/24TB-CRABMAZE1/24TB-CRABMAZE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/29/science/24TB-CRABMAZE1/24TB-CRABMAZE1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/science/24TB-CRABMAZE1/24TB-CRABMAZE1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/science/24TB-CRABMAZE1/24TB-CRABMAZE1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/science/24TB-CRABMAZE1/24TB-CRABMAZE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/29/science/24TB-CRABMAZE1/24TB-CRABMAZE1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/science/24TB-CRABMAZE1/24TB-CRABMAZE1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Happy as a Crab That Just Finished a Maze', 'kicker': 'Trilobites', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Mastering a Labyrinth:  For Some Crabs  In Laboratory Maze,  Right Turns Only   ', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Crabs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Behavior', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Animal Cognition', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labyrinths and Mazes', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Research', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Biology Letters (Journal)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Swansea (Wales)', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pope, Edward', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'your-feed-science', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-24T11:29:42+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Science', 'section_name': 'Science', 'byline': {'original': 'By Veronique Greenwood', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Veronique', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Greenwood', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9be981f9-e4bf-5cd3-86b5-dd9e0f03102c', 'word_count': 628, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9be981f9-e4bf-5cd3-86b5-dd9e0f03102c'}, {'abstract': 'Tina Satter’s remarkable docudrama recreates the bizarrely banal interrogation that led to the arrest of the intelligence contractor Reality Winner.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/24/theater/is-this-a-room-review-reality-winner.html', 'snippet': 'Tina Satter’s remarkable docudrama recreates the bizarrely banal interrogation that led to the arrest of the intelligence contractor Reality Winner.', 'lead_paragraph': 'A lot of what’s being said on the stage of the Vineyard Theater these days is maddeningly ordinary — the kind of friendly, vapid conversation you might exchange with a stranger in a grocery store line. Yet every word spoken, no matter how banal, seems to stretch your nerves closer to snapping.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The N