cif.html', 'snippet': 'Republicans have railed against the secretive nature of the House impeachment inquiry, but that is typical of congressional investigations.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — House Republicans’ move to occupy the secure chambers of the House Intelligence Committee on Wednesday may not have succeeded in shutting down Democrats’ impeachment inquiry. But for a day at least, it shifted debate in the Capitol away from damaging testimony against President Trump to questions about how the inquiry itself is being conducted.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '18', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/24/us/politics/24dc-secret-01/merlin_163190748_dd768a95-bb3f-49ef-9ce1-2a610cfb439b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/24/us/politics/24dc-secret-01/merlin_163190748_dd768a95-bb3f-49ef-9ce1-2a610cfb439b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/24/us/politics/24dc-secret-01/merlin_163190748_dd768a95-bb3f-49ef-9ce1-2a610cfb439b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/24/us/politics/24dc-secret-01/merlin_163190748_dd768a95-bb3f-49ef-9ce1-2a610cfb439b-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/24/us/politics/24dc-secret-01/24dc-secret-01-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/24