: 'nyt://article/7acbf89a-5e8e-5aaa-8dee-d9417a28fe74'}, {'abstract': 'Marilyn Stasio takes time off from her crime fiction column to guide readers through some real-life chronicles of violence, madness and appalling misbehavior.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/25/books/review/true-crime-marilyn-stasio.html', 'snippet': 'Marilyn Stasio takes time off from her crime fiction column to guide readers through some real-life chronicles of violence, madness and appalling misbehavior.', 'lead_paragraph': 'People tend to think of crime and mystery stories as “escapist” literature, a way to hide from the atrocities and absurdities of real life. But crime fiction is my reality. So whenever I want some escapist entertainment, I pick up a book about an actual crime. Lucky for me, people can be reliably wicked, so there are always plenty of these true-crime chronicles of violence, madness and appalling misbehavior.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/27/books/review/27TrueCrime-Stasio/27TrueCrime-Stasio-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 425, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/27/books/review/27TrueCrime-Stasio/27TrueCrime-Stasio-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 425}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/27/books/review/27TrueCrime-Stasio/27TrueCrime-Stasio-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 726, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/27/books/review/27TrueCrime-Stasio/27TrueCrime-Stasio-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1451, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbna