: 'nyt://video/a1a92462-9d49-5bdb-b969-4849dad6788b'}, {'abstract': 'When Elizabeth Strout saw her iconic character walking with a cane, she stopped and took a closer look. Here’s why.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/25/books/review/olive-kitteridge-bestseller-list.html', 'snippet': 'When Elizabeth Strout saw her iconic character walking with a cane, she stopped and took a closer look. Here’s why.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In the first chapter of Elizabeth Strout’s “Olive, Again,” which debuts at No. 6 on this week’s hardcover fiction list, the man who will become Olive’s second husband writes, “Dear Olive Kitteridge, I have missed you and if you would see fit to call me or email me or see me, I would like that very much.”', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '24', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/books/review/03insidethelist-web/03insidethelist-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/03/books/review/03insidethelist-web/03insidethelist-web-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/books/review/03insidethelist-web/03insidethelist-web-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/books/review/03insidethelist-web/03insidethelist-web-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/books/review/03insidethelist-web/03insidethelist-web-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75