f Regrets Leaving', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trump-Ukraine Whistle-blower Complaint and Impeachment Inquiry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Kelly, John F (1950- )', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Mulvaney, Mick', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-26T19:14:21+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Karni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Karni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/42fbf0d3-06c6-504d-90cc-003671044f7a', 'word_count': 599, 'uri': 'nyt://article/42fbf0d3-06c6-504d-90cc-003671044f7a'}, {'abstract': 'The world’s most repressive city is also home to a bizarre array of museums, halls and skyscrapers.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/26/opinion/sunday/architecture-north-korea-pyongyang.html', 'snippet': 'The world’s most repressive city is also home to a bizarre array of museums, halls and skyscrapers.', 'lead_paragraph': 'In July 2015, the two of us stepped off a plane at the newly opened airport in Pyongyang, North Korea. It was our first time in the country. As architects based in Beijing, we were well acquainted with the world’s cities and skyscrapers, but North Korea was a dark spot in our mental map — filled in, as it was for most people, by preconceptions and stereotypes that rendered the so-called Hermit Kingdom in black and white. We had tried to leave those ideas behind, but we didn’t expect that this first visit would leave us with such a sense of confusion, one where the difference between what was real and genuine was muddled by what was ostensibly staged or faked.', 'print_section': 'SR', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/27/opinion/00mit1-12/00mit1-12-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 536, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/27/opinion/00mit1-12/00mit1-12-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 536}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/27/opinion/00mit1-12/00mit1-12-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 915, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/27/opinion/00mit1-12/00mit1-12-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1830, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/27/opinion/00mit1-12/00mit1-12-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/27/opinion/00mit1-12/00mit1-12-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/27/opinion/00mit1-12/00mit1-12-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Pyongyang’s Retro Sci-Fi Architecture', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Pyongyang’s Retro Sci-Fi Architecture', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARCHITECTURE', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'North Korea',