s/dance/crystal-pite-body-and-soul-review.html', 'snippet': 'Audiences seem to love this uneven piece, which can be lyrical in places and bemusing in others.', 'lead_paragraph': 'PARIS — “Body and Soul,” Crystal Pite’s new full-length work for the Paris Opera Ballet, opens in sepulchral gloom, with two Beckettian figures obeying instructions (“right, left, right, left”) from a disembodied voice. It ends with 40 black-latex-clad and masked dancers with insectlike prosthetic arms and protuberances, performing synchronized marches to a hard-driving rock song by Teddy Geiger, while a hairy-headed creature in gold sequined trousers gyrates wildly in the middle.', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '5', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/arts/27pitepix1/merlin_163317540_21b28147-ddb1-4d17-98f9-35dccbc2490c-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 431, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/29/arts/27pitepix1/merlin_163317540_21b28147-ddb1-4d17-98f9-35dccbc2490c-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 431}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/arts/27pitepix1/merlin_163317540_21b28147-ddb1-4d17-98f9-35dccbc2490c-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 735, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/arts/27pitepix1/merlin_163317540_21b28147-ddb1-4d17-98f9-35dccbc2490c-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1470, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/arts/27pitepix1/27pitepix1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name'