Cooley sat alone, having just put on her white uniform for the last time.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '14', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'Leaving Prison at 72', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '‘Not Home Yet, but at Least You’re Free’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Drug Abuse and Traffic', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Mandatory Sentencing', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Probation and Parole', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Tutwiler, Julia, Prison for Women (Wetumpka, Ala)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Cooley, Geneva', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Prisons and Prisoners', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-28T09:00:19+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'National', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'byline': {'original': '', 'person': [], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/edf6fedc-36bd-5772-9c02-d50c4925f2b7', 'word_count': 1451, 'uri': 'nyt://article/edf6fedc-36bd-5772-9c02-d50c4925f2b7'}, {'abstract': 'And it has been this way for almost 50 years.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/28/nyregion/nyc-marathon-wreaths.html', 'snippet': 'And it has been this way for almost 50 years.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Jane Muhrcke tends to walk slowly and carefully these days. Wearing a hard-plastic medical boot on one foot, she has a common injury for runners, a stress fracture on her second metatarsal. But she has never run a mile.', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/nyregion/03WREATHS3/merlin_162925566_18898ea9-b0f4-46a7-90