'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Google Inc', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-28T20:32:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Business', 'section_name': 'Technology', 'byline': {'original': 'By Daisuke Wakabayashi', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Daisuke', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wakabayashi', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c4120319-cc9d-57dc-beb0-124bd6086b88', 'word_count': 601, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c4120319-cc9d-57dc-beb0-124bd6086b88'}, {'abstract': 'When he goes low, Democrats are supposed to go high. Except, it turns out, going low feels wonderful.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/28/opinion/trump-booed-world-series.html', 'snippet': 'When he goes low, Democrats are supposed to go high. Except, it turns out, going low feels wonderful.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Most weeks my Mondays unfold in a well-practiced routine: brush teeth, wash face, walk dog. This morning, I added a new step: spend 15 minutes scrolling through Twitter to see whether anyone had synced that delicious footage of President Trump’s face falling on Sunday — as the World Series crowd is booing him — with the R.E.M. song “Everybody Hurts.”', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '31', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/28/opinion/28Weiner1/merlin_163446129_5f9cc31c-d39e-4afa-9ae0-6c31f20bdfc1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 404, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/28/opinion/28Weiner1/merlin_163446129_5f9cc31c-d39e-4afa-9ae0-6c31f20bdfc1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 404}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/28/opinion/28Weiner1/merlin_163446129_5f9cc31c-d39e-4afa-9ae0-6c31f20bdfc1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 689, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/28/opinion/28Weiner1/merlin_163446129_5f9cc31c-d39e-4afa-9ae0-6c31f20bdfc1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1377, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/28/opinion/28Weiner1/28Weiner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/28/opinion/28Weiner1/28Weiner1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/28/opinion/28Weiner1/28Weiner1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Why Did It Feel So Good to See Trump Booed?', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Trump  Got Booed.  Can I Smile?', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Presidential Election of 2020', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-28T20:41:38+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jennifer Weiner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jennifer', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Weiner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt