eported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/9fa0fda9-dd3a-5186-8b58-eefc6840976c', 'word_count': 803, 'uri': 'nyt://article/9fa0fda9-dd3a-5186-8b58-eefc6840976c'}, {'abstract': 'Major League Baseball staged a routine rehearsal of a World Series title celebration before a game had been played in Washington. Then social media erupted.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/28/sports/baseball/nationals-astros-trophy-curse.html', 'snippet': 'Major League Baseball staged a routine rehearsal of a World Series title celebration before a game had been played in Washington. Then social media erupted.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — It was a routine dress rehearsal, not an inflammatory prediction. A stage was set up in the Nationals Park last week so that Major League Baseball could practice for a trophy presentation as the World Series shifted from Houston with Washington holding a two-games-to-none lead. ', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/28/sports/28series-superstitions-1/merlin_163252203_01e5df1f-85cb-4108-82f8-a99aec5e64de-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/28/sports/28series-superstitions-1/merlin_163252203_01e5df1f-85cb-4108-82f8-a99aec5e64de-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/28/sports/28series-superstitions-1/merlin_163252203_01e5df1f-85cb-4108-82f8-a99aec5e64de-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/28/sports/28series-superstitions-1/merlin_163252203_01e5df1f-85cb-4108-82f8-a99aec5e64de-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/28/sports/28series-superstitions-1/merlin_163252203_01e5df1f-85cb-4108-82f8-a99aec5e64de-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/28/sports/28series-superstitions-1/merlin_163252203_01e5df1f-85cb-4108-82f8-a99aec5e64de-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/28/sports/28series-superstitions-1/merlin_163252203_01e5df1f-85cb-4108-82f8-a99aec5e64de-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'No, the Nationals Are Not Cursed by an Early Plan to Celebrate', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Superstitious Sport, Trophy Rehearsal Turns Into Bad Omen', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Baseball', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'World Series', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Superstitions', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Nationals Park (Washington, DC)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Social Media', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Washington Nationals', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Houston Astros', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Major League Baseball', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-29T00:05:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Sports', 'section_name': 'Sports', 'subsection_name': 'Baseball', 'byline': {'original': 'By James Wagner', 'person': [{'firstname': 'James', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wagner', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/3715554f-d0ea-52e3-8de9-d7e69610e815', 'word_count': 654, 'uri': 'nyt://article/3715554f-d0ea-52e3-8de9-d7e69610e815'}, {'abstract': 'The auction house now sells 12 styles of wine, with price points many can afford.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/28/dining/drinks/sothebys-wine.html', 'snippet': 'The auction house now sells 12 styles of wine, with price points many can afford.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The notion of wine at Sotheby’s brings to mind rare, top-of-the-line collections up for auction. But that doesn’t apply to the auction house’s new line of wines bearing its own label and sold in its wine shop and online. It sells 12 wines, each a well-crafted, almost textbook example of a particular varietal, category and region, without suggesting great age-worthy distinction. They are for dinner, not special occasions, and priced from $16.95 to $39.95. Sotheby’s wine experts, led by Jamie Ritchie, the company’s wine chairman, contacted producers with whom they were familiar and arranged to have some of their wines bottled with the Sotheby’s label. There’s blanc de blancs grand cru Champagne, Prosecco, Sancerre Blanc 2018, Bourgogne Blanc 2016, Sonoma chardonnay 2018, Sancerre rosé 2018, Langhe nebbiolo 2017, Sonoma pinot noir 2017, Bourgogne Rouge 2016, St. Émilion 2017, Pessac-Léognan 2017 and Haut Médoc 2010.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/30/dining/28burner7/merlin_163175712_ec24cf97-6259-4897-abed-971390030c0f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/30/dining/28burner7/merlin_163175712_ec24cf97-6259-4897-abed-971390030c0f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/30/dining/28burner7/merlin_163175712_ec24cf97-6259-4897-abed-971390030c0f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/30/dining/28burner7/merlin_163175712_ec24cf97-6259-4897-abed-971390030c0f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/30/dining/28burner7/merlin_163175712_ec24cf97-6259-4897-abed-971390030c0f-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/30/dining/28burner7/merlin_163175712_ec24cf97-6259-4897-abed-971390030c0f-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/30/dining/28burner7/merlin_163175712_ec24cf97-6259-4897-abed-971390030c0f-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Sotheby’s Has a Wine Label of Its Own', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Serve: Sotheby’s Now Has A Wine Label of Its Own', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Wines', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': "Sotheby's", 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-29T00:09:09+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'subsection_name': 'Wine, Beer & Cocktails', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/8af243ea-20b2-5a94-acba-1ec2c3db33ea', 'word_count': 178, 'uri': 'nyt://article/8af243ea-20b2-5a94-acba-1ec2c3db33ea'}, {'abstract': 'It’s not easy to turn your back on political comrades.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/28/opinion/trump-human-scum-tweet.html', 'snippet': 'It’s not easy to turn your back on political comrades.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m often incredulous at Republican servility to Donald Trump. I’ve struggled to understand how people who’ve spent a lifetime chest-beating about patriotism can be so willing to burn liberal democracy to the ground to protect a man they wouldn’t trust to sell them a used car. So I’ve tried to envision a situation in which I might be tempted to do the same.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '30', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/28/opinion/28goldberg-1/merlin_163145091_da534047-bef3-41da-a7a5-3e71ed202c39-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/28/opinion/28goldberg-1/merlin_163145091_da534047-bef3-41da-a7a5-3e71ed202c39-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/28/opinion/28goldberg-1/merlin_163145091_da534047-bef3-41da-a7a5-3e71ed202c39-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/28/opinion/28goldberg-1/merlin_163145091_da534047-bef3-41da-a7a5-3e71ed202c39-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/28/opinion/28goldberg-1/28goldberg-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/28/opinion/28goldberg-1/28goldberg-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/28/opinion/28goldberg-1/28goldberg-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'In Praise of ‘Human Scum’', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In Praise of ‘Human Scum’', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Impeachment', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Conservatism (US Politics)', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Liberalism (US Politics)', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Flake, Jeffrey L', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Romney, Mitt', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-29T00:14:02+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Michelle Goldberg', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Michelle', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Goldberg', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/da3777e1-906a-5c93-9a84-63372f9ede87', 'word_count': 941, 'uri': 'nyt://article/da3777e1-906a-5c93-9a84-63372f9ede87'}, {'abstract': 'The Other Bar lets the snacker decide how to give back: help a farmer or plant a tree.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/28/dining/the-other-bar.html', 'snippet': 'The Other Bar lets the snacker decide how to give back: help a farmer or plant a tree.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Some high-end chocolates carry the fair trade label from companies that work closely with farmers and support them. But they represent a small percentage of worldwide chocolate production. Now, with the participation of the United Nations Development Program, the FairChain Foundation based in Amsterdam has introduced the Other Bar, made with fine Ecuadorean chocolate, which sells for $2.99 for a package of two. Some of the profits are given back to the farmers. The bars are good quality, with 72 percent cacao for the dark, 50 percent for the milk. In each package there’s a blockchain token you can scan. Use it to make a donation to the farmers, save up four tokens to fund a tree or get 25 cents off your next purchase.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/30/dining/28burner6/28burner6-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 439, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/30/dining/28burner6/28burner6-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 439}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/30/dining/28burner6/28burner6-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 749, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/30/dining/28burner6/28burner6-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1498, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/30/dining/28burner6/28burner6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/30/dining/28burner6/28burner6-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/30/dining/28burner6/28burner6-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'A Chocolate Bar With a Golden Blockchain Token', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Nibble: A Chocolate Bar  That Helps Farmers', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Agriculture and Farming', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Chocolate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Other Bar, The, Inc', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-29T00:14:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/bf741912-3be8-5870-befb-c9a6bbe403fd', 'word_count': 154, 'uri': 'nyt://article/bf741912-3be8-5870-befb-c9a6bbe403fd'}, {'abstract': 'President Barack Obama watched from the Situation Room as commandos went after Osama bin Laden. Eight years later, President Trump watched a raid unfold against Abu Bakr al-Baghdadi.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/28/us/politics/situation-room-photos-trump-obama.html', 'snippet': 'President Barack Obama watched from the Situation Room as commandos went after Osama bin Laden. Eight years later, President Trump watched a raid unfold against Abu Bakr al-Baghdadi.', 'lead_paragraph': 'WASHINGTON — Two images, one filled with tension and action, one static and posed, depict the country’s commanders in chief at significant, and parallel, moments in their presidencies — overseeing missions to capture and kill terrorists long sought by the United States.', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '11', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/28/us/politics/28dc-photos2/28dc-photos2-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/28/us/politics/28dc-photos2/28dc-photos2-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/28/us/politics/28dc-photos2/28dc-photos2-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/28/us/politics/28dc-photos2/28dc-photos2-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/28/us/politics/28dc-photos2/28dc-photos2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/28/us/politics/28dc-photos2/28dc-photos2-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/28/us/politics/28dc-photos2/28dc-photos2-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '2 Photos of Tense White House Moments: Note the Differences', 'kicker': 'NEWS ANALYSIS', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'In a Moment of High Stakes, Two Presidents, Two Approaches', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Obama, Barack', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Photography', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Baghdadi, Abu Bakr al-', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'bin Laden, Osama', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Targeted Killings', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Terrorism', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'White House Building (Washington, DC)', 'rank': 9, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Islamic State in Iraq and Syria (ISIS)', 'rank': 10, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'AL QAEDA', 'rank': 11, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-29T00:14:53+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Annie Karni', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Annie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Karni', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News Analysis', '_id': 'nyt://article/703c33e4-51c3-50c2-ae04-0da42e12a2db', 'word_count': 941, 'uri': 'nyt://article/703c33e4-51c3-50c2-ae04-0da42e12a2db'}, {'abstract': 'In Simon Bajada’s new “Baltic” cookbook, Estonia, Latvia and Lithuania’s food cultures are explored.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/28/dining/baltic-cookbook.html', 'snippet': 'In Simon Bajada’s new “Baltic” cookbook, Estonia, Latvia and Lithuania’s food cultures are explored.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Nordic cuisine has garnered interest recently, but the nearby Baltic States, Estonia, Latvia and Lithuania, also deserve attention. They rely on similar ingredients like fish (especially smoked), potatoes, caraway, cabbage, dairy, and foraged and fermented products. This new, beautifully photographed book that explores their cuisines fine-tunes the character of each. Estonia is the most Nordic of them, there are Russian influences in Latvia, and Lithuania, once an empire, is more diverse, with a Jewish component. The book offers dishes like hearty soups, a hotpot of smoked fish with potatoes and cream, stuffed cabbage, yeasted potato bread, a kugel-like shredded potato dish from Lithuania and Latvian butter seasoned with toasted hemp seeds. Come spring I plan to try fresh cucumbers with honey.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/30/dining/28burner4/28burner4-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 427, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/30/dining/28burner4/28burner4-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 427}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/30/dining/28burner4/28burner4-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 729, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/30/dining/28burner4/28burner4-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1458, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/30/dining/28burner4/28burner4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/30/dining/28burner4/28burner4-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/30/dining/28burner4/28burner4-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'The Baltic States Get Their Culinary Due', 'kicker': 'Front Burner', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'To Cook: The Baltic States  Get Their Culinary Due', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Cooking and Cookbooks', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Latvia', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Lithuania', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Estonia', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Bajada, Simon', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'creative_works', 'value': 'Baltic: New and Old Recipes: Estonia, Latvia & Lithuania (Book)', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-29T00:19:45+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Dining', 'section_name': 'Food', 'byline': {'original': 'By Florence Fabricant', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Florence', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Fabricant', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/4e0382ac-c959-5b4e-9f55-55837c1119d8', 'word_count': 162, 'uri': 'nyt://article/4e0382ac-c959-5b4e-9f55-55837c1119d8'}, {'abstract': 'The seasonings, buoyed by Sichuan peppercorns, chiles and mushrooms, boost savory dishes.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/28/dining/momofuku-seasoned-salts.html', 'snippet': 'The seasonings, buoyed by Sichuan peppercorns, chiles and mushrooms, boost savory dishes.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Flavored salts are not significant in my culinary wardrobe, though occasionally some come along that tempt me, like this set of three developed by Momofuku. A kosher salt blended with crushed Sichuan peppercorns, called Tingly, was the star. The amount of the piquant, palate-numbing spice is well-balanced in the salt, so it does not overwhelm what you season. A ruddy orange salt called Spicy is fueled with several chiles and gives a nice finish to beef and pork. The one labeled Savory blends salt and pepper with umami-rich components like kelp, mushrooms and tamari.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '3', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/30/dining/28burner5/28burner5-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/30/dining/28burner5/28burner5-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/30/dining/28burner5/28burner5-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/30/dining/28burner5/28burner5-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/30/dining/28burner5/28burner5-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 