one, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Sessions, Jefferson B III', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Elections, Senate', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'ALABAMA', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Republican Party', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Jones, Doug (1954- )', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Moore, Roy S', 'rank': 8, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-29T04:35:54+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Washington', 'section_name': 'U.S.', 'subsection_name': 'Politics', 'byline': {'original': 'By Maggie Haberman and Jeremy W. Peters', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Maggie', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Haberman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Jeremy', 'middlename': 'W.', 'lastname': 'Peters', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/2a9769e6-0739-5e96-a0ef-c4d421dc60b0', 'word_count': 544, 'uri': 'nyt://article/2a9769e6-0739-5e96-a0ef-c4d421dc60b0'}, {'abstract': 'Catch Rob Zombie’s unmasking of Michael Myers, and stream an experimental silent film about the history of witchcraft.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/29/arts/television/whats-on-tv-tuesday-rob-zombie-halloween-and-haxan.html', 'snippet': 'Catch Rob Zombie’s unmasking of Michael Myers, and stream an experimental silent film about the history of witchcraft.', 'lead_paragraph': 'HALLOWEEN (2007) 9 p.m. on AMC. In his New York Times review of John Carpenter’s 1978 slasher film “Halloween,” Jason Zinoman wrote that Michael Myers isn’t like other movie monsters: “He never speaks and offers no hint of a motivation for his killing spree. He is not a character so much as an absence of one, an abstraction in the middle of a mundane slice of suburban life.” But this take on that film, directed by the heavy metal singer Rob Zombie, upends that idea by exploring Myers’s back story and unmasking his motive to kill. It follows his childhood as a socially awkward, bullied boy with a stressful home life, which fuels his rage, leading him to enact his first murderous rampage on Halloween night at just 10 years old. He’s then locked away in a mental institution and breaks out 15 years later in an attempt to reconnect with his younger sister, who’s now a teenager. In his review for The New York Times, Matt Zoller Seitz wrote that “the case study part of the film re-establishes Mr. Zombie’s status as modern American horror’s most eccentric and surprising filmmaker.”', 'print_section': 'C', 'print_page': '7', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/arts/29tvcol-halloween/29tvcol-halloween-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/29/arts/29tvcol-halloween/29tvcol-halloween-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/arts/29tvcol-halloween/29tvcol-halloween-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/arts/29tvcol-halloween/29tvcol-halloween-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/a