d46-36372d2fa2d0', 'word_count': 1106, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f33c6b0e-c6a2-5ad9-bd46-36372d2fa2d0'}, {'abstract': 'Meet the people who keep their city running while the rest of the world sleeps.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/29/opinion/India-Mumbai-midnight-gardeners.html', 'snippet': 'Meet the people who keep their city running while the rest of the world sleeps.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Mumbai is to India what New York is to the United States — a gateway to the world and a world within itself, bursting with life, holding the dreams of millions. Many of these Mumbaikers work at night, part of a vast economy that keeps the city running. Because they’re on the job while much of the city is asleep, their efforts go unseen and unnoticed.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [], 'headline': {'main': 'The Midnight Gardeners of Mumbai', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'Mumbai (India)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Labor and Jobs', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-29T19:29:12+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Divya Pathak', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Divya', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Pathak', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/b69a8b15-9789-5788-9a43-72ca7864a7cc', 'word_count': 370, 'uri': 'nyt://article/b69a8b15-9789-5788-9a43-72ca7864a7cc'}, {'abstract': 'Matt Bevin, the unpopular Republican incumbent, has strongly aligned himself with President Trump and invoking impeachment as a cudgel against his opponent, Andy Beshear.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/29/us/politics/matt-bevin-andy-beshear-kentucky-governor.html', 'snippet': 'Matt Bevin, the unpopular Republican incumbent, has strongly aligned himself with President Trump and invoking impeachment as a cudgel against his opponent, Andy Beshear.', 'lead_paragraph': 'GEORGETOWN, Ky. — Addressing a group of Democratic activists last week, Kentucky’s attorney general and nominee for governor, Andy Beshear, flayed his Republican opponent, Gov. Matt Bevin, for his record and his incendiary conduct to argue why voters should oust the incumbent. In the audience here a lawyer wore an oversized “IMPEACH” button, but Mr. Beshear made clear that his concerns were strictly local. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '17', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/us/politics/29kentucky1/merlin_163290525_f5dff525-eec6-45e0-9b54-4e4b3ffc074f-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/29/us/politics/29kentucky1/merlin_163290525_f5dff525-eec6-45e0-9b54-4e4b3ffc074f-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/us/politics/29kentucky1/merlin_163290525_f5dff525-eec6-45e0-9b54-4e4b3ffc074f-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/us/politics/29kentucky1/merlin_163290525_f5dff525-eec6-45e0-9b54-4e4b3ffc074f-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/us/politics/29kentucky1/29kentucky1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/29/us/p