9'}, {'abstract': 'Caveh Zahedi’s abject, self-defeating, ethically questionable, maddeningly original approach to documentary.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/30/magazine/caveh-zahedi-documentary-film.html', 'snippet': 'Caveh Zahedi’s abject, self-defeating, ethically questionable, maddeningly original approach to documentary.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On the fifth episode of Caveh Zahedi’s “The Show About the Show” — a metadocumentary series that is sort of like if “Scenes From a Marriage” were crossed with “Synecdoche, New York” and then filtered through reality TV and the cheerful low-budget atmosphere of public-access cable but also a completely sui generis work of art that is nothing like any of those things and doubles as a deranged social experiment — Zahedi’s wife, Amanda Field, pleads with him to leave something on the cutting-room floor. The context is a little hard to explain; it involves the question of whether reimbursing an actor for the cocaine he snorted is as illegal as buying cocaine for yourself. But Field is upset and wants it out.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '45', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/magazine/03mag-zahedi/03mag-zahedi-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'height': 784, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/03/magazine/03mag-zahedi/03mag-zahedi-articleLarge-v3.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 784}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/magazine/03mag-zahedi/03mag-zahedi-jumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 784, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/magazine/03mag-zahedi/03mag-zahedi-superJumbo-v3.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1568, '