b_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/30/opinion/the-great-pumpkin-peanuts-halloween.html', 'snippet': 'His unwavering belief in the Halloween deity has drawn me to the 1966 “Peanuts” special year after year.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Pop culture can feel like religion when you’re a kid, a shared set of heroes and poses, attitudes, moods and jokes. For my father, who was born in 1933, it was a tone set by the two Franks — Sinatra and Capra. In my formative years, which ran from the mid-1970s to the mid-’80s, my general outlook on life, though fueled by David Letterman and Bruce Springsteen, was anchored by “Peanuts,” the world drawn by the cartoonist Charles Schulz. ', 'print_section': 'A', 'print_page': '29', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/31/opinion/31cohen-1/31cohen-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 444, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/31/opinion/31cohen-1/31cohen-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 444}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/31/opinion/31cohen-1/31cohen-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 757, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/31/opinion/31cohen-1/31cohen-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1515, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/31/opinion/31cohen-1/31cohen-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/31/opinion/31cohen-1/31cohen-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, 