an.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '20', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/magazine/Mag-Hodgman-1/Mag-Hodgman-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 600, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/02/12/magazine/Mag-Hodgman-1/Mag-Hodgman-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 600}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/magazine/Mag-Hodgman-1/Mag-Hodgman-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/magazine/Mag-Hodgman-1/Mag-Hodgman-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/magazine/Mag-Hodgman-1/Mag-Hodgman-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/02/12/magazine/Mag-Hodgman-1/Mag-Hodgman-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/02/12/magazine/Mag-Hodgman-1/Mag-Hodgman-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Judge John Hodgman on Eating Unpeeled Eggs', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Bonus Advice From Judge John Hodgman', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Eggs', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Comedy and Humor', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-31T09:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By John Hodgman', 'person': [{'firstname': 'John', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Hodgman', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/c831689a-91ef-5c3e-912b-b14ff24ba536', 'word_count': 153, 'uri': 'nyt://article/c831689a-91ef-5c3e-912b-b14ff24ba536'}, {'abstract': 'Anticipate sedimentation. Keep the water fresh. Cut any trees by the edge yearly.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/31/magazine/how-to-build-a-moat.html', 'snippet': 'Anticipate sedimentation. Keep the water fresh. Cut any trees by the edge yearly.', 'lead_paragraph': '“Nothing about a moat is easy,” says Hendri Meendering, the general manager of Fort Bourtange, a small fortress in the Netherlands surrounded by a star-shaped moat first built in 1593. Prepare to spend time and money. By the 1970s, the fort was mostly ruined and the moat dry, when the local government began excavating the canals and rebuilding; the project took 25 years and went way over budget. “The canals must be deep and wide,” Meendering says: Try eight feet deep and 20 to 40 feet wide. Consider geology and its potential effects on sedimentation. Plan a route across; Bourtange has five wooden drawbridges, but they’re too heavy and dangerous to pull up. Don’t expect your moat to stop swimmers not wearing armor. “A person can easily swim across within a minute if they want,” Meendering says.', 'print_section': 'MM', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/magazine/03Mag-Tip-1/03Mag-Tip-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 815, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/03/magazine/03Mag-Tip-1/03Mag-Tip-1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 815}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/magazine/03Mag-Tip-1/03Mag-Tip-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 1024, 'width': 755, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/magazine/03Mag-Tip-1/03Mag-Tip-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 2048, 'width': 1509, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/magazine/03Mag-Tip-1/03Mag-Tip-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/03/magazine/03Mag-Tip-1/03Mag-Tip-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/magazine/03Mag-Tip-1/03Mag-Tip-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'How to Build a Moat', 'kicker': 'Tip', 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'How to Build a Moat', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Canals', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-31T09:00:01+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Malia Wollan', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Malia', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Wollan', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/f76d6b64-c004-5749-9918-301ca1fd96f5', 'word_count': 356, 'uri': 'nyt://article/f76d6b64-c004-5749-9918-301ca1