hthora muscae fatally infects house flies, it makes microscopic stalks for hurtling spores at other insects that come nearby.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/31/science/fungus-zombie-flies.html', 'snippet': 'After Entomophthora muscae fatally infects house flies, it makes microscopic stalks for hurtling spores at other insects that come nearby.', 'lead_paragraph': 'The living dead may buzz among us. Attacked by a fungus that takes over their bodies, flies start acting erratically in the moments before they die, playing an unwitting role in spreading the fungus even further. Scientists call them “zombie flies,” and they are found across North America and Europe.', 'print_section': 'D', 'print_page': '2', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/science/29TB-ZOMBIEFLY1/merlin_163536837_448f8228-c94b-40e0-81ed-06d1ae61639a-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 445, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/29/science/29TB-ZOMBIEFLY1/merlin_163536837_448f8228-c94b-40e0-81ed-06d1ae61639a-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 445}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/science/29TB-ZOMBIEFLY1/merlin_163536837_448f8228-c94b-40e0-81ed-06d1ae61639a-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 760, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/science/29TB-ZOMBIEFLY1/merlin_163536837_448f8228-c94b-40e0-81ed-06d1ae61639a-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1520, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/29/science/29TB-ZOMBIEFLY1/29TB-ZOMBIEFLY1-thumbStandard.jpg'