act': 'Anna Meredith has written music for orchestras and choirs. But her latest venture is an album with her band.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/31/arts/music/anna-meredith.html', 'snippet': 'Anna Meredith has written music for orchestras and choirs. But her latest venture is an album with her band.', 'lead_paragraph': 'LONDON — In a cramped, down-at-the-heels rehearsal room, the composer Anna Meredith was frowning at her laptop. In front of her were an electronic keyboard, a sound mixer bristling with knobs, two drums and a toy xylophone. A clarinet on a stand stood on the floor next to an electronic drum pad. After a short pause, Ms. Meredith picked up the clarinet, grimaced and glanced across at her bandmates. “Now, if I could just remember what I’m meant to be doing on this one, that would be terrific,” she said.', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/31/arts/31anna-meredith5/31anna-meredith5-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/31/arts/31anna-meredith5/31anna-meredith5-articleLarge-v2.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/31/arts/31anna-meredith5/31anna-meredith5-jumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/31/arts/31anna-meredith5/31anna-meredith5-superJumbo-v2.jpg', 'height': 1366, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/31/arts/31anna-meredith5/31anna-meredith5-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/31/arts/31anna-meredith5/31anna-meredith5-thumbStandard-v2.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/31/arts/31anna-meredith5/31anna-meredith5-thumbLarge-v2.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'One of Britain’s Top Young Composers (Just Don’t Call Her Classical)', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Meredith, Anna (1978- )', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Music', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Classical Music', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Pop and Rock Music', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-31T15:31:22+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Weekend', 'section_name': 'Arts', 'subsection_name': 'Music', 'byline': {'original': 'By Andrew Dickson', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Andrew', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Dickson', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/d2db8763-4499-5174-958c-c7238f1daf73', 'word_count': 1240, 'uri': 'nyt://article/d2db8763-4499-5174-958c-c7238f1daf73'}, {'abstract': 'The House resolution confirms the developments that will almost definitely end in the president’s impeachment.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/31/opinion/trump-impeachment-inquiry.html', 'snippet': 'The House resolution confirms the developments that will almost definitely end in the president’s impeachment.', 'lead_paragraph': 'On Thursday, five weeks after Speaker Nancy Pelosi announced a formal impeachment inquiry into President Trump, the House adopted a resolution confirming that inquiry. The timing is somewhat confusing: The House has had success in several recent court cases, and there’s nothing in the Constitution or in House rules that requires it to adopt a resolution to conduct an impeachment inquiry. So why now?', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/31/opinion/31huder-1-sub/merlin_163259172_47ced8c0-7ea6-4f56-8858-9dcbc588905d-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 400, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/31/opinion/31huder-1-sub/merlin_163259172_47ced8c0-7ea6-4f56-8858-9dcbc588905d-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 400}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/31/opinion/31huder-1-sub/merlin_163259172_47ced8c0-7ea6-4f56-8858-9dcbc588905d-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 683, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/31/opinion/31huder-1-sub/merlin_163259172_47ced8c0-7ea6-4f56-8858-9dcbc588905d-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1365, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/31/opinion/31huder-1-sub/31huder-1-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/10/31/opinion/31huder-1-sub/31huder-1-sub-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/31/opinion/31huder-1-sub/31huder-1-sub-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Trump Has Received a Formal Invitation to Be Impeached', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Trump-Ukraine Whistle-blower Complaint and Impeachment Inquiry', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'subject', 'value': 'United States Politics and Government', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Democratic Party', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Trump, Donald J', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Pelosi, Nancy', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-31T15:31:30+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'OpEd', 'section_name': 'Opinion', 'byline': {'original': 'By Joshua C. Huder', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Joshua', 'middlename': 'C.', 'lastname': 'Huder', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'Op-Ed', '_id': 'nyt://article/681d537b-3c6b-583d-9818-8afa36fd4592', 'word_count': 885, 'uri': 'nyt://article/681d537b-3c6b-583d-9818-8afa36fd4592'}, {'abstract': 'The inconspicuous landmarks where the Depression exploded, modern art bloomed, and the United Nations first assembled.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/31/nyregion/5-new-york-buildings-that-changed-american-history.html', 'snippet': 'The inconspicuous landmarks where the Depression exploded, modern art bloomed, and the United Nations first assembled.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Can a conglomeration of bricks, glass, wood, steel and mortar reveal the soul of a city? Maybe even a country? Forged from natural resources and assembled by human ingenuity, these buildings help illustrate how New York evolved from struggling Dutch company town into world capital. There are 700,000 buildings in the city. Here are five of the more inconspicuous yet important ones, along with the events that made them famous. ', 'print_section': 'MB', 'print_page': '1', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/nyregion/03BUILDINGS1/03BUILDINGS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 441, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/03/nyregion/03BUILDINGS1/03BUILDINGS1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 441}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/nyregion/03BUILDINGS1/03BUILDINGS1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 753, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/nyregion/03BUILDINGS1/03BUILDINGS1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 1506, 'width': 2048, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/nyregion/03BUILDINGS1/03BUILDINGS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/03/nyregion/03BUILDINGS1/03BUILDINGS1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/nyregion/03BUILDINGS1/03BUILDINGS1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': '5 New York Buildings That Changed American History', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': 'Five Buildings Where History Was Made', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'ARMORY SHOW, THE INTERNATIONAL FAIR OF NEW ART (NYC)', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Hunter College', 'rank': 2, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'Lehman College', 'rank': 3, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'United Nations', 'rank': 4, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'organizations', 'value': 'House of Representatives', 'rank': 5, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'persons', 'value': 'Friedman, Milton', 'rank': 6, 'major': 'N'}, {'name': 'glocations', 'value': 'New York City', 'rank': 7, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-31T15:41:14+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Metropolitan', 'section_name': 'New York', 'byline': {'original': 'By Sam Roberts', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Sam', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Roberts', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/795caf62-6429-501d-87a6-6b1440053fad', 'word_count': 1679, 'uri': 'nyt://article/795caf62-6429-501d-87a6-6b1440053fad'}, {'abstract': 'A painter who loved mystical colors blurring, earth to sky, might have liked a vividly descriptive poem which holds a long-ago moment as a hinge for everything to come.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/31/magazine/poem-remembering-the-night-i-dreamed-paul-klee-married-the-sky.html', 'snippet': 'A painter who loved mystical colors blurring, earth to sky, might have liked a vividly descriptive poem which holds a long-ago moment as a hinge for everything to come.', 'lead_paragraph': 'I’m fond of the fact that, beyond the title, Paul Klee does not appear in Jack Ridl’s luminous poem at all. I think Klee might have liked that, too. A painter who loved mystical colors blurring, earth to sky, might have liked a vividly descriptive poem which holds a long-ago moment as a hinge for everything to come. “It was just that we knew,” is one of those wondrous, instinctive lines containing everything. How rare is an evening like this? How possible? That couple in their 60s might have seemed old then, but they were so alive, so aware. I am crazy about those napkins. Selected by Naomi Shihab Nye', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/magazine/03mag-poem-1/03mag-poem-1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 245, 'width': 364, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/magazine/03mag-poem-1/03mag-poem-1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 245, 'width': 364, 'subType': 'superJumbo', 'crop_name': 'superJumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbnail', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/magazine/03mag-poem-1/03mag-poem-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'height': 75, 'width': 75, 'subType': 'thumbnail', 'crop_name': 'thumbStandard', 'legacy': {'thumbnail': 'images/2019/11/03/magazine/03mag-poem-1/03mag-poem-1-thumbStandard.jpg', 'thumbnailwidth': 75, 'thumbnailheight': 75}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'thumbLarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/magazine/03mag-poem-1/03mag-poem-1-thumbLarge.jpg', 'height': 150, 'width': 150, 'subType': 'thumbLarge', 'crop_name': 'thumbLarge', 'legacy': {}}], 'headline': {'main': 'Poem: Remembering the Night I Dreamed Paul Klee Married the Sky', 'kicker': None, 'content_kicker': None, 'print_headline': '', 'name': None, 'seo': None, 'sub': None}, 'keywords': [{'name': 'subject', 'value': 'Poetry and Poets', 'rank': 1, 'major': 'N'}], 'pub_date': '2019-10-31T15:41:26+0000', 'document_type': 'article', 'news_desk': 'Magazine', 'section_name': 'Magazine', 'byline': {'original': 'By Jack Ridl and Naomi Shihab Nye', 'person': [{'firstname': 'Jack', 'middlename': None, 'lastname': 'Ridl', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 1}, {'firstname': 'Naomi', 'middlename': 'Shihab', 'lastname': 'Nye', 'qualifier': None, 'title': None, 'role': 'reported', 'organization': '', 'rank': 2}], 'organization': None}, 'type_of_material': 'News', '_id': 'nyt://article/db984761-f869-5825-bb0a-066ee50cc344', 'word_count': 280, 'uri': 'nyt://article/db984761-f869-5825-bb0a-066ee50cc344'}, {'abstract': 'The troubled German bank alerted federal authorities to a transaction in which it sold a stake in a California office complex to a company linked to the son of a former Kremlin official.', 'web_url': 'https://www.nytimes.com/2019/10/31/business/deutsche-bank-russia-real-estate-deal.html', 'snippet': 'The troubled German bank alerted federal authorities to a transaction in which it sold a stake in a California office complex to a company linked to the son of a former Kremlin official.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Deutsche Bank was already under federal investigation for helping wealthy Russians launder money when it struck a deal last year to sell a property it co-owned in California.', 'print_section': 'B', 'print_page': '4', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/31/business/31deutsche2/merlin_155279061_41da4f51-c53c-421d-bc6b-dffbcebb183b-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 393, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/10/31/business/31deutsche2/merlin_155279061_41da4f51-c53c-421d-bc6b-dffbcebb183b-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 393}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/10/31/business/31deutsche2/merlin_155279061_41da4f51-c53c-421d-bc6b-dffbcebb183b-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 671, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type'