/books/review/10-new-books-we-recommend-this-week.html', 'snippet': 'Suggested reading from critics and editors at The New York Times.', 'lead_paragraph': 'Happy Day of the Dead, everyone. Let’s get right to the scary stuff. This week we recommend Joe Hill’s new collection of horror stories, “Full Throttle,” along with tales of capital punishment (Fiona Kidman’s “This Mortal Boy”), Nazi war criminals (Joseph Kanon’s “The Accomplice”) and thorny cosmic deities (“The New Annotated H. P. Lovecraft,” edited by Leslie S. Klinger). Those should keep you reading deep into the night while you wait for your Halloween sugar rush to wear off. We also have a couple of books about felonious women — one of them fictional (Hannelore Cayre’s “The Godmother”) and one of them not (Doris Payne’s “Diamond Doris,” about her career as a jewel thief) — and, for good measure, two poetry collections, a novel about a French chef and a tribal history of the Lakota people stretching from the 16th century to the present. Any of those would be right at home on the ofrenda for a particularly literate ancestor.', 'print_section': 'BR', 'print_page': '23', 'source': 'The New York Times', 'multimedia': [{'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'xlarge', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/books/03edchoice1/03edchoice1-articleLarge.jpg', 'height': 285, 'width': 600, 'subType': 'xlarge', 'crop_name': 'articleLarge', 'legacy': {'xlarge': 'images/2019/11/03/books/03edchoice1/03edchoice1-articleLarge.jpg', 'xlargewidth': 600, 'xlargeheight': 285}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'jumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/books/03edchoice1/03edchoice1-jumbo.jpg', 'height': 487, 'width': 1024, 'subType': 'jumbo', 'crop_name': 'jumbo', 'legacy': {}}, {'rank': 0, 'subtype': 'superJumbo', 'caption': None, 'credit': None, 'type': 'image', 'url': 'images/2019/11/03/books/03edchoice1/03edchoice1-superJumbo.jpg', 'height': 891, 'width': 1875, 'subType': 'sup